\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Open Mixed; Singapore Dollar Down On Yen \b0\par\par\uc2 469 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 1999\par 01:40\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG -(Dow Jones)- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are mixed against the U.S. dollar in quiet dealing as Asian trading hours begin Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Overnight activity in New York saw the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought up against the Singapore dollar, as the U.S. dollar's moderate rally against the yen squeezed market players running short positions in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the Singapore dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar market tends to show an asymmetric relationship with trading in the yen, with the U.S. dollar mirroring its moves upward against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  while downward moves against the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar are limited by fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the local \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At 0015 GMT (7:15 p.m. Wednesday EST), the U.S. dollar was quoted against the Singapore dollar at S$1.6825, down from an overnight high of S$1.6830 but still above S$1.6782 late in Asia the previous day. \par \par \uc2  Against the Indonesian rupiah, the U.S. dollar was at IDR7,295, compared with IDR7,260 late the previous day. \par \par \uc2  With heavy investor interest to sell dollars detected at IDR7,500, and good dollar buying interest at levels between IDR7,200 and IDR7,000, the dollar is likely to remain within a broad range against the rupiah over the short to medium term, say dealers. \par \par \uc2  "It's just going to drift sideways over the next few weeks, unless something really drastic happens," commented a Singapore-based broker. \par \par \uc2  With separatist tensions rising in various Indonesian provinces, however, few market participants are prepared to rule out a violent upswing in rupiah volatility. \par \par \uc2  Dealing in the baht is subdued so far. Against the Thai baht, the U.S. dollar was quoted at THB38.9100, up from THB38.8800 late the day before. \par \par \uc2  Trading on the Philippine Dealing System is due to open at 0100 GMT. At the close of trading Wednesday, the U.S. dollar was at PHP40.935. \par \par \uc2  The outlook for North Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains highly favorable, according to most analysts. Following a batch of positive inflation and trade data released in Seoul Wednesday, the won is generally expected to appreciate, although government-directed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to boost the U.S. dollar over the short term \par \par \uc2  Trading in the won is set to start at 0030 GMT. At Wednesday's close, the dollar was trading at KRW1,157.30. \par \par \uc2  Official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also expected to slow the ascent of the New Taiwan dollar, which hit a fresh two-year high Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Domestic dealing in Taipei is scheduled to begin at 0100 GMT. At the end of Wednesday's session, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted against the New Taiwan dollar at NT$31.669. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 852 2832 2341; tom.holland@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dvc208999\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
