\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Flat Against US Dlr; Range-Trading Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 200 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 1999\par 03:10\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar is flat against the U.S. dollar early Thursday in what is expected to be a day of rangebound trading. \par \par \uc2  At 0200 GMT (9:00 p.m. EST Thursday), the U.S. dollar was at S$1.6796, unchanged from late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that the market is consolidating after the U.S. dollar's sudden drop against the Singapore dollar two days ago. \par \par \uc2  Because of the aggressive selloff Tuesday, "The market is afraid to buy (U.S. dollars) beyond S$1.6830," said a dealer at an American bank in Singapore. "It's a psychological resistance level." \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar's weakness against the yen is also expected to limit any gains against the Singapore dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0209 GMT, the dollar was trading at Y102.57, below Y102.72 in New York late Wednesday. The dollar was quoted at Y102.18 late in Tokyo Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  On the other hand, expectations of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , are supporting the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the level of about S$1.6650, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dvc2089ag\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
