\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  -  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  tempers won, Taiwan dlr. \b0\par\par\uc2 940 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 November 1999\par 11:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Nov 26 (Reuters) - Dollar buying by the Korean \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par authorities tempered the won's\tab     recent bull run on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  Friday, while the Singapore government's moves to tweak \par \par \uc2  restrictions on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to have any immediate \par \par \uc2  impact. \par \par \uc2      Elsewhere, \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  held on to their easier bias partly \par \par \uc2  due to dollar short-covering ahead of the weekend though the \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par yen\tab     looked set to revisit recent highs amid growing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bullishness about Japan.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The euro grabbed the limelight, falling to all time lows\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par against the yen\tab \tab  and hovering near 4-month lows\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par against the dollar below $1.0150.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Traders in Tokyo said the already bearish euro had suffered\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par after European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  board member Eugenio Domingo Solans\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said the bank had no intention of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SOUTH KOREAN WON\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dollar buying by the monetary authorities and expectations\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par they would curb any won rise kept dollar/won in a tight range\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par despite won purchases by foreign stock funds.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The market was kept on tenter-hooks from early on, after\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the government expressed "deep concern" over the won's strength\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and said it was ready to take action.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But Seoul traders said the dollar was unlikely to hold onto\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par its gains due to more expectations for foreign stock purchases,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar sales by offshore players and month-end export deals.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Traders saw a 1,152-1,162 range for Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Disappointment over a sharp sell-off in stocks weighed on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the Taiwan dollar after institutional investors turned net\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sellers in the TAIEX\tab    on jitters over relations with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par China.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But last minute \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cushioned the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Taiwan dollar's fall, showing players the authorities were\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par staying true to their pledge to defend the exchange rate at any\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sign of trouble.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Unsubstantiated rumours of Chinese military deployment off\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Taiwan sent already bearish stocks reeling to a close of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 7,595.44, down nearly four percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SINGAPORE DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Plans unveiled by the government to liberalise the use of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the Sing dollar to bolster local capital markets had no\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par discernible impact on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , with analysts saying the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par move would only have longer-term results.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The government announced a relaxation of rules governing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par foreigners' use of the Sing dollar for bond, equity, interest\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rate and repurchase agreement transactions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts said the moves fell short of internationalising\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , partly because no move had been made to ease\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par existing limits on Sing dollar swap trade.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "In the long-term, (the policies) could create more demand\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . But it's not a key issue determining the Sing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar right now," said Anand Aithal, regional strategist at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Goldman Sachs in Singapore.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THAI BAHT\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The baht slipped on corporate dollar demand as debtors were\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par spooked by the yen's bullish trend and rushed to repay debt on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fears it could rise further.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht's fall was somewhat amplified by thin volume,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Bank of Thailand said on Friday it planned to peg\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par monetary policy to inflation targets and thereby stabilise the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par baht and manage the economy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Under the new system, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would set an\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inflation target for two years.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     A national monetary policy comprising central bankers and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par independent experts would then change interest rates to keep\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inflation within the target.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso drooped as market participants continued to cover\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par short dollar positions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  took third quarter growth figures in its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stride as they were mostly in line with the market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expectations.     June-September GDP growth came in at 3.1\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent year-on-year versus 3.6 percent in the second quarter.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     On the ballooning fiscal deficit, a concern among\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par investors, Socio-economic Planning Secretary Felipe Medalla\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said the government must adopt a tighter fiscal policy next\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Medalla said the government should keep the deficit below\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 62.5 billion pesos next year as the gap this year could be as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par high as 90 billion pesos.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Persistent demand for dollars ahead of year-end pushed the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rupiah to around 7,200, with dealers expecting pressure to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par remain due to Y2K worries and political uncertainties.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par They said the market's focus was still on separatist\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pressure in the province of Aceh, with some analysts fearful of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par possible disintegration in Indonesia if the country breaks\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par free.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The government has decided not to impose martial law and to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par try and resolve differences through dialogue.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     HONG KONG DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The government released GDP data showing the economy grew\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 4.5 percent year-on-year in the third quarter, well above\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market forecasts of two to four percent growth.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     It also revised its 1999 growth forecast to 1.8 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from 0.5 percent previously.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ...Latest bid....Prev Close....Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Ringgit......3.7995.......3.8000.........0.01%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Rupiah......7180.00......7185.00.........0.07%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Baht..........38.81........38.70.........-0.28%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Peso..........40.77........40.67.........-0.25%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Sing dlr.....1.6720.......1.6700.........-0.12%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Taiwan dlr...31.725.......31.680.........-0.14%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Korean won..1159.30......1158.00.........-0.11%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen....104.11.......104.45.........0.33%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change since start of Asia crisis\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .....Latest......July '97......Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Ringgit......3.7995.......2.5200........-33.68%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Rupiah......7180.00......2432.00......