\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Slightly Down Early; Follows Yen, Regionals \b0\par\par\uc2 166 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 November 1999\par 02:40\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar is slightly weaker in quiet dealing early Friday, taking its direction from the yen and other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  About 0125 GMT (8:25 p.m. Thursday EST), the U.S. dollar was at S$1.6720, up from S$1.6707 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was at Y104.40, up slightly from Y104.23 in London late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Weakness in the Thai baht and Indonesian rupiah will also support the U.S. dollar against the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  is another factor supporting the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Thursday, the MAS was said to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy U.S. dollars between the levels of S$1.6680 and S$1.6700, dealers said. The MAS declined to comment. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect the U.S. dollar to trade in a range of S$1.6700 to S$1.6735 Friday. \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dvbq085bf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
