\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Down Late; Seen Up On 3rd Quarter Econ Data Thursday \b0\par\par\uc2 296 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 November 1999\par 11:37\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar is weaker against the U.S. dollar in late trading Wednesday on selling by offshore market participants amid thin trading volume, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At about 1019 GMT (5:19 a.m. EST), the U.S. dollar was at S$1.6697, up from S$1.6683 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide against the U.S. dollar was in part due to cross trading in the Indonesian rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Recent optimism about the repatriation of flight capital from wealthy Indonesian Chinese, who placed many of their funds in Singapore, sparked buying in the rupiah, and the selling of Singapore dollars. \par \par \uc2  However, many participants are saying the U.S. dollar's rise against the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is capped by upcoming third quarter gross domestic product figures that are expected to show Singapore's economy continuing along a strong growth path. \par \par \uc2  The scheduled release Thursday at 0000 GMT (7:00 p.m. EST) of the economic data also kept most participants sidelined Wednesday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  A Dow Jones Newswires survey of eight economists said the economy will grow by 6.9%, up from 6.7% a year ago. \par \par \uc2  "People are expecting the figure to be pretty good and the Sing dollar should strengthen," said a dealer at a U.S. banking house. \par \par \uc2  However, any rise to S$1.6660 will likely trigger \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  In the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  money market, the overnight rate was offered at 1.2500%, down from 1.6875% from Tuesday, while offers for the three-month rate fell to 2.750% from 2.875%. \par \par \uc2  -By Bernice Han; 65-421-4800; bernice.han@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dvbh08321\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
