\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Regains Ground To End Higher Vs US Dollar \b0\par\par\uc2 327 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 November 1999\par 10:18\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar ended slightly stronger against the U.S. dollar Thursday after bouncing back from intraday lows of around S$1.6725 to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  About 0905 GMT (4:05 a.m. EST), the U.S. dollar was at S$1.6663, down from S$1.6677 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar's weakness against the Singapore dollar shadowed its decline against the Indonesian rupiah and Thai baht, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to find support just below S$1.6600, the level at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  is said to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent days. \par \par \uc2  "The market is still looking to sell (U.S. dollars) but at this level they are worried about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the authorities," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Now that the Indonesian presidential election is over, the market will turn its attention to Singapore's strong economic fundamentals, likely resulting in a strengthening of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in coming weeks, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which in the past has tried to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in order to foster Singapore's economic recovery, will now allow it to appreciate, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  However, they added, the MAS won't allow the Singapore dollar to rise too fast. "They will still try to moderate the fall" of the U.S. dollar, a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The market may try to test the lower end of the U.S. dollar's trading range against the Singapore dollar during London and New York trading hours, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The market is still a touch long," a dealer at a foreign bank said. "(The) dollar-Sing (Singapore dollar) may test the downside again." \par \par \uc2  In the local money market, the overnight rate was offered at 2.000%, up from 1.875% late Wednesday, while the three-month rate was offered unchanged at 2.8125%, its highest level this year. \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dvb407ud9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
