\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dlr Down Late Vs US$ On Rumored MAS  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 218 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 November 1999\par 09:54\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  -(Dow Jones)- The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar has weakened against the U.S. dollar late Tuesday on rumored \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but observers say the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is poised to strengthen further by the end of the year. \par \par \uc2  At 0835 GMT (3:35 a.m. EST), the U.S. dollar was at S$1.6679, up from S$1.6605 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the MAS came in to squeeze U.S. dollar short positions out of the market in a bid to temper the recent strength of the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has been trading at 10-month highs. \par \par \uc2  The MAS has admitted to entering the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to smooth any moves it considers unwarranted. \par \par \uc2  But dealers note the MAS will be more tolerant toward a gradual appreciation of the Singapore dollar to S$1.6500 to the U.S. dollar by the end of the year, in light of recent strength in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the yen, and building inflationary pressures. \par \par \uc2  In the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  money market, the overnight rate was offered at 1.875%, below 2.250% from late Monday, while the three-month rate was offered unchanged at 2.6875%. \par \par \uc2  -By Anita Jain; 65-421-4807; anita.jain@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument d