\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Stronger Late; Trading At 10-Mo Highs \b0\par\par\uc2 266 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 November 1999\par 10:04\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar is sharply stronger against the U.S. dollar late Monday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  finds a higher range as regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rise, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At about 0940 GMT (4:40 a.m. EST), the U.S. dollar was at S$1.6605, down from S$1.6682 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar has risen to 10-month highs as the Indonesian rupiah and the Thai baht continue to gather strength, the rupiah particularly bolstered by the prospect of a return to political and economic stability, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  After bursting through a resistance level of S$1.6590 to the U.S. dollar early Monday, the Singapore dollar rose to an intraday high of S$1.6575 to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at a U.S. bank said the Singapore dollar will now trade around S$1.6575-S$1.6600 against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said, however, they haven't seen any signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which monitors the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against a trade-weighted basket. \par \par \uc2  The dealer at the U.S. bank said an abrupt move in the markets could spark MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is frequently aimed at quelling \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar strength in the interest of export competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  In the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  money market, the overnight rate was offered unchanged at 2.250% from late Friday, while the three-month rate was offered at 2.6875%, also unchanged. \par \par \uc2  -By Anita Jain; 65-421-4807; anita.jain@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dvb107sl3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
