\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  - Regionals up on hopes of inflows. \b0\par\par\uc2 787 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 November 1999\par 02:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      0127 GMT - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  mostly edged up in early Monday \par \par \uc2  trading, buoyed by expectations of increased capital inflows. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The yen\tab     resumed strength against the dollar after a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sizeable dollar sell-off in New York despite a sparkling\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par performance in U.S. asset markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said the yen gains were driven by Japan's recovery\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par story, hopes of a higher fiscal stimulus package and the Bank\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of Japan's reluctance to pursue quantitative easing.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The market was divided over the policy direction of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. Federal Reserve in the near-term.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Some believed the Fed might be done raising rates after\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par boosting rates twice in the summer. Others said the National\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Association of Purchasing Management index to be released on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Monday and October U.S. payroll data on Friday might set the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par scene for further tightening at next week's policy meeting.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par *** The rupiah\tab   was firmer as the market expected the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par International Monetary Fund and the World Bank to resume\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lending from Indonesia's $45 billion international bail-out\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par package.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indonesia's new chief economics minister Kwik Kian Gie said\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on Friday he was confident the IMF and World Bank would resume\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the much-needed lending to Indonesia.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The IMF suspended new loans to the country pending the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par resolution of the Bank Bali scandal. IMF Asia-Pacific director\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Hubert Neiss is due in Jakarta on Tuesday for talks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par *** The baht\tab   gained some ground against the dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par after monthly economic data released on Friday showed a rise in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par exports and a relatively strong current account surplus.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Thailand's Commerce Ministry is scheduled to release\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par October inflation data at 0400 GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Although the market expects the data to show some uptick\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par due to a surge in oil prices, the overall figures are likely to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par be mild because of last year's high base.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     *** The Australian dollar\tab     slipped after the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par country's trade deficit for September came in higher than\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expected.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The balance of goods and services for September hit a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par record high of A$1.939 billion deficit against a median\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expectation of a A$1.4 billion deficit and August's A$1.3\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par billion deficit.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par *** The peso\tab   was hovering at 40 per dollar, with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par domestic financial markets closed on Monday and Tuesday for the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par All Saints Day and All Souls' Day holiday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has cut the official overnight borrowing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rate to 8.75 percent from nine percent, with effect from this\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par week. The overnight lending rate remains at 11 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par *** The Taiwan dollar\tab   was a shade firmer, with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Taipei dealers expecting more upside due to steady inflows from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par foreign equity funds and persistent strength in the yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Foreign funds were net buyers of T$2.29 billion worth of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Taiwan stocks on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Taipei dealers see it trading in a range of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par T$31.725-T$31.75 due to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's policy to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par against sharp moves in either direction.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     *** The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar\tab     was firmer, in line with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the brighter regional mood.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Deputy Prime Minister Lee Hsien Loong was quoted as saying\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore's third quarter economic growth may be slightly lower\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par than the strong 6.7-percent performance in the second quarter.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Official Q3 data is due to be released in November.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     *** The South Korean won\tab     opened lower on Monday but\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rebounded soon after, supported by carried-over export\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par settlement deals and $150 million worth of inflows for stock\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par investments.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The country's October trade figures showed the trade\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par surplus of $2.15 billion versus $2.99 billion a year ago.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Exports rose 27 percent year-on-year while imports were up 48.5\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The October Producer Price Index and foreign reserves data\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par are due at 0400 GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ...Latest bid....Prev Close....Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Ringgit......3.7995.......3.8000.........0.01%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Rupiah......6730.00......6885.00.........2.30%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Baht..........38.59........38.72.........0.34%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Peso..........40.00........40.18.........0.45%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Sing dlr.....1.6614.......1.6665.........0.31%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Taiwan dlr...31.680.......31.730.........0.16%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Korean won..1196.00......1199.50.........0.29%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen....104.19.......104.91.........0.69%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change since start of Asia crisis\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .....Latest......July '97......Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Ringgit......3.7995.......2.5200........-33.68%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Rupiah......6730.00......2432.00........-63.86%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Baht..........38.59........25.90........-32.88%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Peso..........40.00........26.50........-33.75%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Sing dlr.....1.6614.......1.4300........-13.93%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Ta