\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Open Up In Response To Dollar Weakness \b0\par\par\uc2 244 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Oktober 1999\par 03:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG -(Dow Jones)- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have opened stronger against the dollar in Asian trading Monday, following the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide in the major \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in European and U.S. hours Friday. \par \par \uc2  Brokers in Singapore report relatively heavy interest to sell the dollar against \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  across the region, with early sales of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  seen in the interbank market against the rupiah, the baht and the Singapore dollar. \par \par \uc2  At 0045 GMT (8:45 p.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar is quoted against the Indonesian rupiah at 7,850, compared with IDR8,050 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  Against the Thai baht, the U.S. dollar is quoted at 39.10, down from THB39.26 late in Friday's session. \par \par \uc2  Against the Singapore dollar the U.S. dollar is quoted at 1.6745, compared with S$1.6777 late in Asia Friday. Fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  should support the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  above S$1.6700 for the time being. \par \par \uc2  Against the South Korean won, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has opened at 1,204.80, down from KRW1,206.00 at the previous close. \par \par \uc2  Trading in the Philippine peso and the New Taiwan dollar has yet to begin. At Friday's close the U.S. dollar was at PHP40.330 and NT$31.769. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 852 2832 2341; tom.holland@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dvai07jtr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
