\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Up Slightly Early;Market Awaits Wed BOJ Mtg \b0\par\par\uc2 302 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Oktober 1999\par 03:57\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar is up slightly against the U.S. dollar early Tuesday as the session promises to be calm ahead of Wednesday's Bank of Japan policy meeting, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At about 0145 GMT (9:45 p.m. EDT Monday), the U.S. dollar was at S$1.6748, down from S$1.6783 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar followed the Thai baht's gains against the U.S. dollar. The U.S. dollar was at 39.695 baht at 0145 GMT, down from THB39.860 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expect the Singapore dollar to trade in a tight range as the market awaits the outcome of the Bank of Japan meeting Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  An easing of monetary policy would spark a rally in the U.S. dollar against the yen. The Singapore dollar and other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  would then follow the yen downward, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  If the dollar moves above Y108, then it would rise to the level of S$1.6815, said a dealer at a U.S. bank in Singapore. But, he sees S$1.6850 as the top for the U.S. dollar in the near term regardless of what happens in Japan. \par \par \uc2  The bottom for the U.S. dollar is set by the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which generally is seen to act through local banks. One dealer at a U.K. bank said local banks are buying U.S. dollars at S$1.6750. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar-Sing is getting toward the bottom of its range," the dealer said. "I wouldn't want to be getting short down there." \par \par \uc2  -By Christopher Wellisz; 65 421-4802; 