\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  -2: MAS  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Fuels S$ Weakness \b0\par\par\uc2 294 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 1999\par 10:34\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  At 0800 GMT (4:00 a.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar was trading at Y107.52, down from Y107.85 in late Asian trading Thursday, but well up from Y107.01 in overnight trading Thursday. The euro was trading at $1.0694, down from $1.0711 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was also trading at $1.6796 Singapore dollars, up from S$1.6788 in late Asian trading Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  is behind current U.S. dollar strength, following indirect \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  through the Development Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "DBS started buying U.S. dollars around S$1.6740 late Thursday," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at a U.S. bank in Singapore. "We believe the MAS is much more comfortable with the Singapore dollar at current levels." \par \par \uc2  He said traders are finding it difficult to sell U.S. dollars, and expects the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to head toward S$1.69 next week. \par \par \uc2  "But given the volatility seen this week, traders are testing the highs and lows, to see what the market will take," he said. \par \par \uc2  At 0800 GMT, the U.S. dollar was trading against the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 7,760 rupiah, up from IDR7,735. Traders said a thin market has made rupiah moves relatively volatile, and that nothing much should be read into rangey moves up or down. \par \par \uc2  "The market is well supported between IDR7,500 and IDR7,800; politics is key, and we should be in for a heck of ride over the next few weeks," a trader at a U.K. bank said, referring to the run-up to the presidential election Oct. 20. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 08-10-99 \par \par \uc2  0834GMT \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dva807c1h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
