\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Lose Ground Early To Resurgent US Dollar \b0\par\par\uc2 341 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 1999\par 03:01\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have lost ground to the U.S. dollar in early trading Friday, as the U.S. dollar remains relatively firm against the yen and the euro, following the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to leave interest rates unchanged. \par \par \uc2  At 0040 GMT (8:40 p.m. EDT Thursday), the U.S. dollar was trading at Y107.14, down from Y107.85 in late Asian trading Thursday but above an overnight low of Y107.01. The euro is trading at $1.0715, almost unchanged from $1.0714 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar is also trading at 39.93 baht, well up from THB39.395, following the break of a key resistance level at THB39.50, traders said. Traders have been saying all week that knee-jerk U.S. dollar selling had been overdone, following the Bank of Thailand's announcement that offshore baht lending would be capped at THB50 million for each financial institution. They said THB40.20 - the level before the announcement - would likely be hit during today's session. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was also trading at 1.6790 Singapore dollars, almost unchanged from $1.6788. Traders said the U.S. dollar was pushed higher late Thursday by indirect \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; they said the Development Bank of Singapore started to buy U.S. dollars aggressively at S$1.6740. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar is also trading at 7,788 Indonesian rupiah, just up from IDR7,733 in late Asian trading Thursday. \par \par \uc2  On the Philippine dealing system, the U.S. dollar is quoted at 40.32 pesos, flat against PHP40.325 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  In north Asia, the U.S. dollar is trading at 1,202.8 Korean won, up from KRW1,201 late Thursday. The U.S. dollar is also quoted at 31.78 New Taiwan dollars, unchanged from late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  -By Brian Truscott; 65 421 4800;brian.truscott@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 08-10-99 \par \par \uc2  0101GMT \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dva807bmh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
