\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dlr Weaker Late On Suspected MAS  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 207 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 1999\par 11:12\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar has weakened against the U.S. dollar late Thursday on what dealers say could be selling on behalf of local monetary authorities. \par \par \uc2  At about 0850 GMT, the U.S. dollar was at S$1.6793, up from S$1.6778 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at a U.S. bank said he believes a "stealth \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped push the U.S. dollar past the S$1.6800 mark to an intraday high of S$1.6815 before it fell back to current levels. \par \par \uc2  The MAS steps into the market to smooth moves it sees as excessive or unwarranted. In past months, it has entered the market to stem the Singapore dollar's rise in an effort to preserve export competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  The dealer said the Singapore dollar has been strong all week on program-based buying by institutions. \par \par \uc2  In the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  money market, the overnight rate was offered unchanged at 2.000% from late Wednesday, while the three-month rate was offered at 2.500%, also unchanged. \par \par \uc2  -By Anita Jain; 65-421-4807; anita.jain@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 07-10-99 \par \par \uc2  0912GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dva707a9x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
