\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Higher As Yen Strength Appears Capped \b0\par\par\uc2  By Brian Truscott \par \uc2 256 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 September 1999\par 10:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were stronger against the U.S. dollar in late Asian trading Monday, buoyed by signs that the Japanese yen's future strength would be capped by domestic and international \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders and economists said. \par \par \uc2  The Group-of-Seven leading industrialized countries showed cautious support for Japan and its ongoing struggle with \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets during a meeting in the U.S. Saturday. G7 finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors said in a communique that they "shared Japan's concern about the potential impact of the yen's appreciation for the Japanese economy and the world economy." \par \par \uc2  Jimmy Koh, regional economist at IDEA Global.com in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said the prospect of joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets is therefore a step closer and that could create a self-fulfilling prophesy in how the yen strengthens or weakens in coming weeks. \par \par \uc2  He added that Bank of Japan Governor Masaru Hayami's comments over the weekend underpinned the argument because the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is prepared to provide ample liquidity if yen strength becomes a factor. \par \par \uc2  "His comments shows that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not only looking at interest rates but \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength," he said, adding that the U.S. dollar should move to Y106 to Y108 in the near term. At 0800 GMT, the U.S. dollar was trading at Y104.16, down a touch from Y104.43 earlier Monday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 27-09-99 \par \par \uc2  0830GMT \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv9r06z8x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
