\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  -3: Peso Dn Despite Good Economic Data \b0\par\par\uc2 437 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 1999\par 11:48\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  On the Philippine Dealing System, the U.S. dollar was also trading at 40.165 pesos, up from PHP39.935 late Wednesday. Traders said the U.S. dollar rebound and simmering tensions in Indonesia have pushed the peso down, even though there are increasing signs the country is experiencing an economic resurgence. In the seven months to July, the Philippines posted a trade surplus of $755 million, compared with a $1.44 billion deficit in the same period last year. \par \par \uc2  "Besides the won, the peso is also looking relatively cheap at levels over PHP40 (to the U.S. dollar)," IDEA Global.com's Baweja said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was trading at S$1.6931, well up from $1.6887 late Wednesday. Traders said nothing fundamental had changed with respect to the Singapore dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The U.S. dollar moved higher against the Singapore dollar, in line with the gains made against the other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a trader at a U.S. investment house in Singapore said, adding there are no signs of direct or indirect \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was also trading at 8,110 rupiah, up a touch from IDR8,050 late Wednesday. An extremely thin market - precipitated by ongoing tension related to East Timor as well as fallout from the ongoing Bank Bali scandal involving an illegal transfer of funds - has sidelined much of the market. \par \par \uc2  Indonesian President B.J. Habibie said Thursday that he has asked the Attorney General to thoroughly investigate the banking scandal and prosecute any wrongdoers. The president also appealed to the public to put the scandal in proportion, saying it shouldn't be allowed to damage the bank recapitalization program. \par \par \uc2  Against the Thai baht, the U.S. dollar was trading at THB39.795, up from THB39.4250 late Wednesday. The U.S. dollar managed to hit a 12-month high of THB39.92 in intraday trading before slipping back on profit-taking, traders said, adding ongoing demand for U.S. dollars to pay for offshore debts has been placing downward pressure on the baht. \par \par \uc2  Thailand's deputy finance minister, Pisit Leeahtam, said earlier Thursday that the government was unconcerned by any move in the dollar above THB40, as long as it was in line with the value of other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In other trading, the U.S. dollar was quoted at NT$31.745, down a touch from NT$74.755 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  -By Brian Truscott; 65 421 4800; brian.truscott@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 16-09-99 \par \par \uc2  0948GMT \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv9g06th7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
