\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA MARKETS - Unscathed by early yen  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2      By Tamora Vidaillet \par \uc2 954 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 1999\par 11:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Sept 10 (Reuters) - Japanese efforts to tame the \par \par \uc2  volatile yen on Friday were largely shrugged off by Asian \par \par \uc2  regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while stocks were mixed amid a spate of \par \par \uc2  domestic factors. \par \par \uc2      Most regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained firm despite early \par \par \uc2  dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of Japan, with most of \par \par \uc2  the day's trade dominated by short-covering of local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  positions ahead of the weekend. \par \par \uc2      "Movements on the yen really haven't been the key driver \par \par \uc2  behind \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  like the rupiah, Thai baht and Philippine \par \par \uc2  peso just now," said David Simmons, regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  strategist at Citibank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2      "Only the won and the Singapore dollar (have) seen some \par \par \uc2  movement in line with the yen," Simmons told Reuters \par \par \uc2  Television. \par \par \uc2      RUPIAH JUMPS ON POSITION SQUARING \par \par \uc2      The rupiah bounced back to levels seen at the start of the \par \par \uc2  week as players who had gone long of dollar/rupiah amid the \par \par \uc2  escalating violence in East Timor closed off their positions \par \par \uc2  ahead of the weekend. \par \par \uc2      Players adopted a wait-and-see stance as violence in East \par \par \uc2  Timor showed few signs of abating and as international threats \par \par \uc2  to delay financial aid to Indonesia were stepped up. \par \par \uc2      Thousands may have died in the wave of killing and arson in \par \par \uc2  East Timor, much of it blamed on rampaging pro-Jakarta militia, \par \par \uc2  in the days since the territory's vote for independence was \par \par \uc2  announced. \par \par \uc2      The rupiah's thin trading environment was likely to mean \par \par \uc2  continued volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts said. \par \par \uc2      "It's a pretty stressful experience when ones sees the \par \par \uc2  rupiah gyrating between 7,900 to 9.000 and most of the way back \par \par \uc2  again," said Citibank's Simmons. \par \par \uc2      "But I am sure there will some pockets of demand for U.S. \par \par \uc2  dollars on these sorts of dips, on the back of the continued \par \par \uc2  uncertainties," he said. \par \par \uc2      PESO NUDGES BACK THROUGH 40 LEVEL \par \par \uc2      The Philippine peso pared losses seen earlier this week, \par \par \uc2  firming to the right side of 40 per dollar. \par \par \uc2      But the peso -- which has lost heavily against the dollar \par \par \uc2  amid fears over East Timor -- soon edged back to levels \par \par \uc2  encouraged by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the regional mood brightened. \par \par \uc2      Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Rafael Buenaventura said \par \par \uc2  earlier in the day that the peso should revert to the 39 per \par \par \uc2  dollar level as regional tensions eased. \par \par \uc2      "There is no reason for the peso to go beyond that level," \par \par \uc2  he said, referring to the 40-per-dollar level. \par \par \uc2      Buenaventura also threw water over his earlier hints that \par \par \uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might adjust its overnight floating rate to \par \par \uc2  woo investors into Treasury bills. \par \par \uc2      He said the policy-making Monetary Board had opted to keep \par \par \uc2  its key overnight rates steady at a weekly meeting. \par \par \uc2      THAI Q2 GDP SEEN HIGHER \par \par \uc2      The baht was firmer ahead of expected capital inflows \par \par \uc2  arising from Standard Chartered Bank's acquisition of \par \par \uc2  Nakornthon Bank. \par \par \uc2      Thailand's economy grew about eight percent over the year \par \par \uc2  to the second quarter of 1999, according to a government think \par \par \uc2  tank. \par \par \uc2      A senior finance ministry official quoted the National \par \par \uc2  Economic and Social Development Board as saying Thailand's \par \par \uc2  second quarter performance might raise growth for 1999 to about \par \par \uc2  six percent against a 9.4 percent contraction in 1998. \par \par \uc2  MALAYSIA PUT ON POSITIVE RATING OUTLOOK \par \par \uc2  Malaysian stocks were unimpressed by an upgrade in the \par \par \uc2  country's credit outlook by ratings agency FITCH IBCA. \par \par \uc2  Fitch put Malaysia on rating alert positive which could \par \par \uc2  lead to a sovereign upgrade and said the country was ahead of \par \par \uc2  its Asian neighbours in restructuring its banks and corporate \par \par \uc2  debt. \par \par \uc2  Fitch now sees Malaysia's economy expanding as much as five \par \par \uc2  percent this year, after a contraction of 7.5 percent last \par \par \uc2  year. \par \par \uc2      Malaysia's short and long term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is rated at \par \par \uc2  BBB minus. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par \uc2   Change on the day FRI 10 0844GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .....Latest bid....Prev Close.....Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7998.......3.8000.........0.01% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah.......8275.00......8600.00..