even-month peak of S$1.6639 Aug. 10, largely as a result of the sharp slide in the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Violence in East Timor following a referendum in favor of independence from Indonesia has aroused international condemnation and concerns that economic aid may be suspended. The dollar breached the key IDR9,000 level midmorning, before it fell back to IDR8,970. \par \par \uc2  At 0326 GMT (11:26 p.m. EDT Wednesday), the U.S. dollar was at S$1.6935, up slightly from S$1.6930 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 09-09-99 \par \par \uc2  0331GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv9906m3o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
