\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  - Weaker yen, Timor pressure regionals. \b0\par\par\uc2 846 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 September 1999\par 12:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      1000 GMT - Most regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were easier in late \par \par \uc2  Asian trade as worries over East Timor persisted and as the yen \par \par \uc2  held on to its weaker bias. \par \par \uc2      The yen was seen pressured by some position-squaring ahead \par \par \uc2  of Japan's April-June GDP numbers due on Thursday. \par \par \uc2      A Reuters survey on Wednesday showed that economists had \par \par \uc2  lowered their GDP forecasts after capital spending data for \par \par \uc2  Japanese companies for the same period showed a larger than \par \par \uc2  expected decline. \par \par \uc2      Japan's GDP number, due on Thursday, is now forecast to \par \par \uc2  contract about 0.35 percent compared with the previous quarter. \par \par \uc2      Bank of Japan Governor Masaru Hayami said on Wednesday that \par \par \uc2  a recent rise in the yen and in Tokyo stocks was largely due to \par \par \uc2  foreign buying. He also said that \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements would \par \par \uc2  eventually return to previous levels if excessive. \par \par \uc2  *** The rupiah was lower despite government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as \par \par \uc2  martial law and a shoot-on-sight curfew in East Timor showed no \par \par \uc2  signs of halting the widespread violence. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Syahril Sabirin said the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  but \par \par \uc2  admitted that it was having little impact. \par \par \uc2      He said the government's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  target was still in the \par \par \uc2  range of 6,000 to 7,000 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2      Australian Foreign Minister Alexander Downing said that \par \par \uc2  only U.N. peacekeepers could restore order in East Timor, where \par \par \uc2  militias have massacred hundreds since locals voted for \par \par \uc2  independence last week. \par \par \uc2  But Indonesian State Secretary Muladi ruled out accepting \par \par \uc2  foreign peace-keepers, saying the country would have to deal \par \par \uc2  with the problem alone until the vote for independence is \par \par \uc2  ratified by Indonesia's highest legislative body at its October \par \par \uc2  meeting. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's parliament is expected to receive preliminary \par \par \uc2  results on possible insider dealing in Bank Bali shares next \par \par \uc2  week. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's Supreme Audit Agency and PriceWaterHouse \par \par \uc2  Coopers had said on Tuesday that they had discovered evidence \par \par \uc2  of irregularities in their investigation of a fee payment by \par \par \uc2  Bank Bali to a ruling Golkar party official. \par \par \uc2  *** Worries over East Timor also weighed on the baht, as \par \par \uc2  some players switched out of regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  into the \par \par \uc2  dollar, traders said. \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said on Wednesday that the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's drop to levels not seen since October 1998 was \par \par \uc2  largely due to the weakening yen and the Finance Ministry's \par \par \uc2  comments condoning a weaker baht. \par \par \uc2      Deputy Prime Minister Supachai Panitchpakdi also said the \par \par \uc2  baht's present levels were good for exports. \par \par \uc2      *** The peso fell to its lowest close in 10 months, \par \par \uc2  pressured by weakness in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and in line with \par \par \uc2  the baht. \par \par \uc2      Manila dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's plan to change its \par \par \uc2  overnight borrowing scheme to make Treasury bills more \par \par \uc2  attractive also weighed on sentiment. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Rafael Buenaventura said he might \par \par \uc2  adjust the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's floating rate for overnight borrowing \par \par \uc2  to encourage banks to invest in T-bills. \par \par \uc2      Buenaventura said he saw no need for dollar-selling \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  or for interest rate readjustments to prop up the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\tab "This is more of a knee-jerk reaction to the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thai baht problem," he said, adding that the peso was likely to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par return to the 39 level once volatility in regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par faded.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     *** The won ended lower as players built up dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par positions amid regional jitters.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Seoul traders said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was likely to trade in a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par tight range against the dollar on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Revised International Monetary Fund predictions for South\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Korea's GDP growth were ignored.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     According to preliminary data published on the Dutch\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par finance ministry's web site, the IMF raised its forecast for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par South Korea's annual GDP growth to 6.5 percent from 2.0\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par *** The Taiwan dollar softened with the yen, slipping as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par T$31.864 per dollar before late \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  propped it up.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     *** The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar was easier, weighed down by the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par troubles in East Timor.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Singapore's close trade, investment and political ties with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indonesia mean its markets often suffer with signs of trouble\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in Indonesia. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day WED 08 1002GMT\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ...Latest bid....Prev Close....Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Ringgit......3.7995.......3.8000..........0.01%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Rupiah......8580.00......8260.00.........-3.73%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Baht..........39.33........38.90.........-1.09%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Peso..........40.13........39.75.........-0.95%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Sing dlr.....1.6925.......1.6895.........-0.18%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Taiwan dlr...31.840.......31.837.........-0.01%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Korean won..1194.00......1193.00.........-0.08%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen....110.92.......110.83.........-0.08%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change since start of Asia crisis\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 