\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  -3: S$ Safe Haven; IDR Too Volatile \b0\par\par\uc2 250 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 September 1999\par 10:50\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was also trading at S$1.6832, up slightly from S$1.6821 late Wednesday. Traders said Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was protected in part by its regional safe haven status, given the volatility of the Thai baht and Indonesian rupiah. \par \par \uc2  "The market is comfortable at these levels; when we start getting down toward S$1.68, traders look for signs of (\b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a trader at a U.K. bank in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was also trading at IDR7,775, up a touch from IDR7,707 Wednesday. Traders dismissed any thoughts that many investors were taking a punt on the outcome of the East Timor referendum, expected next week, or what would happen in the run-up to the November presidential elections. \par \par \uc2  "Check the wind direction; that will tell you the same thing, " said one trader. "Trading volumes are low and the prospects for volatility are high over the next week." \par \par \uc2  There are also further signs of economic distress in the country. A government official reported Thursday that non-oil and gas exports fell 13.8% in July, primarily on the back of a decline in the export of agricultural commodities. The government plans on releasing Indonesia's consumer price index Friday. \par \par \uc2  In Taiwan, the U.S. dollar was trading at NT$31.825, almost unchanged from NT$31.83 Thursday. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 02-09-99 \par \par \uc2  0850GMT \par \par \uc