\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  - Mixed amid wary yen, rupiah wobbly. \b0\par\par\uc2 724 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 August 1999\par 04:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      0200 GMT - Regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were looking mixed in early \par \par \uc2  trade, with the dollar slipping against the yen on speculative \par \par \uc2  sales. \par \par \uc2      But the market was cautious about selling the greenback too \par \par \uc2  aggressively below 111 yen due to lingering concerns over \par \par \uc2  possible yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of Japan. \par \par \uc2      Japan's Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs \par \par \uc2  Haruhiko Kuroda said in Singapore on Sunday that the yen's \par \par \uc2  premature appreciation was undesirable. \par \par \uc2      Kuroda was attending a meeting of Manila Framework member \par \par \uc2  countries to discuss Asia's economic crisis. \par \par \uc2      Separately, Japan's former Vice Minister for International \par \par \uc2  Affairs Eisuke Sakakibara told Japanese television on Sunday \par \par \uc2  that the United States and Japan would discuss the weak dollar \par \par \uc2  at a G7 deputies meeting in September. \par \par \uc2  *** The rupiah was weaker amid lingering concerns about the \par \par \uc2  Bank Bali scandal and as voting in East Timor's independence \par \par \uc2  referendum got underway. \par \par \uc2  The IMF said on Sunday that the next disbursement of funds \par \par \uc2  for Indonesia depended on satisfactory settlement of the Bank \par \par \uc2  Bali case. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia has promised an independent audit of its \b \highlight22\uc2 central \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the wake of the scandal which centres on payment of a \par \par \uc2  large fee by Bank Bali to a firm run by an official of the \par \par \uc2  ruling Golkar party to recover loans from the Indonesian Bank \par \par \uc2  Restructuring Agency (IBRA). \par \par \uc2  All eyes are also on the U.N.-organised independence vote \par \par \uc2  in East Timor on Monday. President Clinton has warned \par \par \uc2  Indonesian President B.J.Habibie that ties with Washington \par \par \uc2  would be seriously damaged and that foreign aid could be \par \par \uc2  curtailed if the recent violence escalates. \par \par \uc2  *** The won was easier after posting solid gains against \par \par \uc2  the dollar in late Friday trade as banks unwound dollar \par \par \uc2  positions after accepting export-linked documents from Daewoo \par \par \uc2  Group companies. \par \par \uc2  On Sunday, South Korea reported a 33.1 percent annual jump \par \par \uc2  in industrial output for July compared with a 14.0 percent \par \par \uc2  decline a year earlier. \par \par \uc2  July production was also 2.3 percent higher than in June. \par \par \uc2  The rise was spurred by growing demand for goods both \par \par \uc2  domestically and internationally, especially for automobiles \par \par \uc2  and semiconductors. \par \par \uc2  *** The Philippine peso was holding up ahead of a \par \par \uc2  government auction of Treasury bills which should show if a \par \par \uc2  decision to allow yields to rise will boost the faltering \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The government said on Friday it would allow Treasury bill \par \par \uc2  yields to rise to help restore the premium on local interest \par \par \uc2  rates after last week's U.S. rate hike. \par \par \uc2  Shrinking interest rates spreads and uncertainty over the \par \par \uc2  domestic rate outlook pushed the peso to nine-month lows last \par \par \uc2  week. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Rafael Buenaventura said on Friday \par \par \uc2  the decision to allow higher T-bill rates had reduced the need \par \par \uc2  for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to hike overnight rates or bank reserve \par \par \uc2  requirements. \par \par \uc2  *** The Singapore dollar was a shade easier in light trade. \par \par \uc2  Deputy Prime Minister Lee Hsien Loong said on Sunday that \par \par \uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  should reflect underlying economic fundamentals as \par \par \uc2  the best way to detract speculative pressures. \par \par \uc2  Singapore operates a managed float system, keeps its \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within a certain band to make sure exports remain \par \par \uc2  competitive. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar rose to a seven-month high against the \par \par \uc2  dollar at around 1.66 in early August, with some traders \par \par \uc2  suspecting \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  (MAS) to stem its gains. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par \uc2   Change on the day MON 30 0204GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...Latest bid....Prev Close....Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7995.......3.8000..........0.01% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......7670.00......7500.00.........-2.22% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........38.25........38.26..........0.03% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........39.60........39.68..........0.20% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.6876.......1.6862.........-0.08% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr...31.790.......31.850..........0.19% \par \par \uc2   Korean won..1185.50......1182.00.........-0.30% \par \par \uc2   Japan yen....111.00.......111.41..........0.37% \par \par \uc2   Change since start of Asia crisis \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .....Lates