\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Higher Late; Mkt Takes New Shorts Vs US Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 228 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 August 1999\par 11:16\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar has strengthened slightly against the U.S. dollar late Friday, as market participants slowly begin taking new short positions against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At about 0845 GMT (4:45 a.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar was at S$1.6880, down from S$1.6910 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier this week to stem the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise flushed out many short U.S. dollar positions, and left market players wary of adopting new short positions lest the MAS come into the market again, a dealer at a U.K. bank said. \par \par \uc2  "A lot of people were sufficiently burned by the MAS and won't initiate fresh shorts," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  But he said at present levels, market participants are getting a bit bolder about putting back their short U.S. dollar positions. \par \par \uc2  He said, with little domestic news on the horizon, the Singapore dollar is likely to follow the yen's movements closely next week. \par \par \uc2  In the local-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  money market, the overnight rate was offered at 1.500%, up from 1.250% late Thursday, and the three-month rate was offered at 2.625%, up from 2.375%. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 27-08-99 \par \par \uc2  0916GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv8r06dyj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\pic