\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-S'pore rates seen benign after hike in U.S. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mantik Kusjanto \par \uc2 519 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 August 1999\par 10:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Aug 25 (Reuters) - Singapore interest rates are likely to remain benign in the medium-term despite a 25-basis point hike in the U.S. on Tuesday, analysts said on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS) was expected to continue with its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar competitive, which in turn would induce liquidity in the system, they said. \par \par \uc2  "It's a fact that capital inflows are coming back again as the stock market recovers," Vincent Low, fixed-income strategist at Merrill Lynch, said. \par \par \uc2  "The MAS would keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from appreciating and therefore, its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will probably keep interest rates capped, or even on a downward bias," Low added. \par \par \uc2  The MAS had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in the last couple of days to prevent the Singapore dollar from appreciating too much against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  The move had increased liquidity in the banking system and resulted in interbank rates falling. \par \par \uc2  Some said there was no reason for the Sing dollar to have strengthened to 1.67 recently against the U.S. dollar as it was not warranted on a trade-weighted basis. \par \par \uc2  By 0710 GMT on Wednesday, the Singapore dollar was trading around 1.6918 against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark three-month interbank rate softened to 2.375 percent at Wednesday's fixing from a high of 2.625 percent about two weeks ago, the highest since mid-January 1999. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said the rates were trending up on nervousness in the Asian financial markets, fears of a U.S. rate hike and tension in North and South Asia. \par \par \uc2  Cheong Kwok Mun, analyst at GK Goh, said Singapore interest rates were unlikely to move up in line with U.S. rates. \par \par \uc2  The city-state was just coming out of a recession unlike the U.S., which had been booming for several years. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, the U.S. Federal Reserve raised the federal funds rate for overnight loans between banks and the less-used discount rate by a quarter percentage point each. \par \par \uc2  It also kept an open-minded or "neutral" position on the interest rate outlook, reassuring investors who had feared the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might lean toward additional increases in borrowing costs by adopting a formal tightening "bias." \par \par \uc2  The Fed had also nudged rates higher at its most recent meeting on June 30. Tuesday was the first time in more than five years the Fed had boosted rates at two consecutive meetings. \par \par \uc2  Low said Merrill's view was that there would not be anymore rate hikes for the rest of the year. \par \par \uc2  "The pressure point has been released already. I think it ought to benefit the stock market," he said, adding Singapore's economic recovery was likely to gather momentum. \par \par \uc2  Merrill raised its forecast for Singapore's GDP growth to 6.3 percent in 1999, up from 4.4 percent previously. \par \par \uc2  ((Singapore Newsroom +65 870 3843, Fax +65 776 8112 singapore.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv8p01yhf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\