\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Weaker Early In Tandem With Yen Slip Vs US$ \b0\par\par\uc2 164 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 August 1999\par 04:12\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar is weaker early Tuesday in tandem with the Japanese yen's decline against the U.S dollar. \par \par \uc2  About 0159 GMT (9:59 p.m. Monday EDT), the U.S. dollar was at S$1.6858, up from S$1.6722 late Tuesday. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also at Y112.42, up from Y111.47 in New York late Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expect quiet trading in Singapore ahead of Tuesday's meeting of the U.S. Federal Reserve Board's Open Market Committee, which is widely expected to raise the key federal funds rate by 25 basis points. \par \par \uc2  Rumored \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gained in response to positive trade figures, is also keeping the market cautious, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  -By Christopher Wellisz; 65/421-4802; christopher.wellisz@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 24-08-99 \par \par \uc2  0212GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv8o06733\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
