\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar Follows Yen Upward VS U.S. Dlr Early \b0\par\par\uc2 209 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 August 1999\par 04:09\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar is following the yen upward against the U.S. dollar early Thursday, dealers said, but they suspect its gains are being capped by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At about 0140 GMT, the U.S. dollar was at S$1.6745, down from S$1.6773 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was at around Y111.65, down from Y111.90 in New York late Wednesday and from Y113.87 late Wednesday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar is also getting some support from Wednesday's rally on the Stock Exchange of Singapore, which saw the key Straits Times Index jump 3.3%, and from firmer regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  However, dealers suspect that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore, which is said to be worried about hurting exports, has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  and sold \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollars. \par \par \uc2  "A lot of local banks are buying U.S. dollars at S$1.6730," said a dealer at a European bank. He said local banks were selling in to the New York market late Wednesday, just as the U.S. dollar was falling to half-year lows against the yen. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 19-08-99 \par \par \uc2  0209GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv8j065lc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
