\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  -3: Rupiah, Baht, Peso Higher Late \b0\par\par\uc2 274 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 August 1999\par 11:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The rupiah ended higher following Bank Indonesia's move to hold interest rates steady at Wednesday's auction of short-term \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  paper; the first time rates haven't fallen since March. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia's announcement that the funds irregularly transferred from Bank Bali to a company run by a senior Golkar official had been recovered also bolstered sentiment, which was badly damaged last week by the banking scandal and falling rates. \par \par \uc2  In late trading, the U.S. dollar was quoted at IDR7,255, down from IDR7,360 late Wednesday. Strong support for the dollar is seen at IDR7,000. \par \par \uc2  Against the Thai baht, the U.S. dollar slipped to THB38.3250, down from THB38.3600 late in Asia the day before. \par \par \uc2  Against the Philippine peso, the U.S. dollar ended the local session at PHP39.545, down from PHP39.610 at Thursday's close. \par \par \uc2  After dropping to an intraday low of S$1.6720 against the Singapore dollar, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  recovered as traders covered themselves, nervous of prompting \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to strengthen the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at levels around S$1.6700. \par \par \uc2  "The MAS isn't in the market at the moment, but I don't think the authorities would let the (U.S.) dollar fall below that level," said a trader in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  Toward the end of local interbank trading, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was at S$1.6767, up from S$1.6750 the day before. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 852 2832 2341; tom.holland@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 19-08-99 \par \par \uc2  0958GMT \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv8j06580\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
