\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Higher As Long US Dlr Positions Liquidated \b0\par\par\uc2 293 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 August 1999\par 03:51\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar is stronger against the U.S. dollar in early trading Monday, as investors liquidate long U.S. dollar positions across the region, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "The strong performance on Wall Street Friday means it should be a good day for regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and equity markets," said a trader at a U.S. investment bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  The Dow Jones Industrial Average climbed 184.26 points Friday to close at 10973.65 points, after U.S. economic data showed that inflationary pressures remained nascent. \par \par \uc2  In early trading Monday, the Singapore Straits Times Index is already up 2.2% or 43.24 points to 2012.92 points. \par \par \uc2  At 0145 GMT (9:45 p.m. EDT Sunday), the U.S. dollar was trading at S$1.6728, down from S$1.6740 in late Asian trading Friday. \par \par \uc2  "The U.S. dollar has more room to fall during the session - possibly through S$1.67," said a trader at a Japanese bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  He cautioned that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  could indirectly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market by asking local banks to buy U.S. dollars. Despite the prospect of such U.S. dollar support, signs that Singapore's economic resurgence continues paves the way for a weaker U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  "We could see S$1.62 in the next two months," the trader at the U.S. bank said. \par \par \uc2  In the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  money market, the overnight offer rate on the Singapore dollar was 1.5%, up from 1.0% Friday. The three-month rate remains unchanged at 2.625%. \par \par \uc2  -By Brian Truscott; 65 421 4800; brian.truscott@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 16-08-99 \par \par \uc2  0151GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv8g061m8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
