\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Inch Up Late In Mkts Rocked By Rumors \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tom Holland \par \uc2 271 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 August 1999\par 10:59\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  - \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--Tumbling regional stock markets, heightened tensions between China and Taiwan and fresh expectations that China will devalue the yuan combined to rock Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  during regional trading hours Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Although the majority of Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  actually ended local trading hours higher on the day, traders and analysts warned that rumors will continue to rattle regional markets for the foreseeable future. \par \par \uc2  "People are very quick to take advantage of this sort of rumor. The market just loves the volatility," said Chia Woon Khien, treasury economist at Skandinaviska Enskilda Banken in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  successfully supported the new Taiwan dollar, despite heavy selling pressure prompted by market rumors - speedily denied by Taipei - that Chinese warplanes had crossed into Taiwanese airspace. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the strength of the yen continued to hold the Singapore dollar up, the South Korean won edged higher on favorable trade flows, and the Philippine peso recovered slightly from the 4.5-month lows seen Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht and the Indonesian rupiah both ended Asian hours lower. \par \par \uc2  Regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  came under selling pressure during the Asian morning in response to a Hong Kong newspaper report that China's State Planning Committee is urging Beijing to adopt a "more flexible" yuan policy in a bid to boost exports. Traders took "more flexible" as a clear euphemism for a possible devaluation. \par \par \uc2  The pressure was then redoubled early in the Asian afternoon when a rumor swept the market that Chinese jets had infringed Taiwan's airspace. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 05-08-99 \par \par \uc2  0859GMT \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv8505wo2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
