\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Stronger Early, Follows Yen's Gains Vs US$ \b0\par\par\uc2 228 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 August 1999\par 04:08\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar is slightly stronger against the U.S. dollar early Thursday, tracking the yen's gains against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At about 0140 GMT (9:40 p.m. Wednesday EDT), the U.S. dollar is at S$1.6750, down from S$1.6785 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  With the U.S. dollar falling toward the level of Y114, the Singapore dollar is gaining, dealers said. Those who expected the U.S. dollar to hold near Y115 Wednesday were caught off-guard, a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "It looks like the market is caught long (U.S.) dollar," the dealer said. But he predicted that the U.S. dollar would test the level of S$1.6700 in the course of the day. \par \par \uc2  Another dealer said local banks could start buying the U.S. dollar at S$1.6700, providing some support. "There is fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " to cap the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar's rise at that level, the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  On the local money market, the overnight interbank rate was offered at 2.250%, up from 1.500% late Wednesday in Asia, and the three-month rate was offered at 2.500%, up from 2.250% late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  -By Christopher Wellisz; 65 421-4802 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 05-08-99 \par \par \uc2  0208GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv8505vg2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
