\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Up Late; MAS Seen Unlikely To Enter Market \b0\par\par\uc2 278 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 August 1999\par 11:13\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar is higher against the U.S. dollar late Monday as the yen's rise against the dollar puts upward pressure on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0850 GMT (4:50 a.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.6796, lower than S$1.6864 late Friday and S$1.6824 earlier Monday. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at a U.K. bank said since the Singapore dollar's rise has been steady without any sudden swings and has been largely in tandem with the yen's climb, it is unlikely the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore will step in to quell the Singapore dollar. \par \par \uc2  The de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected last week to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice to stem the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise. \par \par \uc2  The dealer said were the MAS to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , market forces would soon buoy the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar back to its current levels. \par \par \uc2  "The MAS would have its hands full with any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. "There are no dollar bulls." \par \par \uc2  Diminishing fears of an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of Japan to damp the yen's strength are also supporting the Singapore dollar, the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was quoted at Y114.25 late Monday, down from 115.20 late Friday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  On the local money market, the interbank overnight rate was offered at 1.500%, down from 2.000% late Friday in Asia, while the three-month rate was offered at 2.250%, unchanged from late Friday. \par \par \uc2  -By Anita Jain; 65-421-4807; anita.jain@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 02-08-99 \par \par \uc2  0913GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv8205r25\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
