\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Mixed Early But Seen Rising Vs Weak Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 324 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 August 1999\par 03:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are mixed against the U.S. dollar early in local trading hours Monday, but with the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  looking weak against the yen, most traders see the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthening over the course of the coming sessions. \par \par \uc2  At 0045 GMT (8:45 p.m. Sunday EDT), the U.S. dollar is quoted at S$1.6840 against the Singapore dollar, down from S$1.6864 late Friday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  Should the U.S. dollar remain soft against the yen, and should forthcoming corporate results in Singapore reflect the island state's recent buoyant economic performance, dealers see the Singapore dollar strengthening this week. \par \par \uc2  While some traders are wary of \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the U.S. dollar at levels around S$1.67, others expect the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to drop as low as S$1.66 this week. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar is quoted at 37.1750 Thai baht, up from THB37.1200 late in the previous session. With strong resistance capping the market at THB37.30, the U.S. dollar is likely to fall to test support at THB36.90, a trader at a Thai bank in Singapore said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar is at 6,875 Indonesian rupiah, compared with IDR6,835 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has opened at 1,204.70 South Korean won, up slightly from KRW1,204.00 at the previous close. \par \par \uc2  Trading in the Philippine peso and the New Taiwan dollar has yet to begin. At Friday's close in Manila, the U.S. dollar was at 38.250 pesos. At the end of Saturday's session in Taipei, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was at NT$32.145, down from NT$32.192 Friday. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 852 2832 2341; tom.holland@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 02-08-99 \par \par \uc2  0100GMT \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv8205pmh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
