\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Steady Late; Trade Slows After Choppy Wk \b0\par\par\uc2 239 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Juli 1999\par 11:03\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar was barely changed against the U.S. dollar late Friday, as trading slowed after a choppy week. \par \par \uc2  At 0835 GMT (4:35 a.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.6864, slightly weaker from S$1.6870 late Thursday and S$1.6910 earlier Friday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore is believed to have stepped into the market twice in the past week to curb the Singapore dollar's rise. \par \par \uc2  But trading was listless Friday as market participants remained wary of MAS action, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at a U.K. bank noted some slight downward pressure on the U.S. dollar, however, as a result of the U.S. dollar's slide against the yen. \par \par \uc2  He said he expected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar's strength capped at S$1.6750 next week, and S$1.6900 to provide support for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , on the U.S. dollar's weakness against the yen and other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  On the local money market, the overnight interbank rate was offered at 2.000%, up from 1.750% late Thursday in Asia, and the three-month rate was offered at 2.250%, up from 2.1875% late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  -By Anita Jain; 65-421-4807; anita.jain@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 30-07-99 \par \par \uc2  0903GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv7u05ri4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal