\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dlr Weaker Late On Suspected MAS  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 267 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juli 1999\par 11:07\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is weaker late Thursday against the U.S. dollar after an apparent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by monetary authorities to stem the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise. \par \par \uc2  At 0845 GMT (4:45 a.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.6870, higher than both S$1.6820 seen late Wednesday and early Thursday's S$1.6775, the level at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore is believed to have stepped into the market to support the slumping U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Early Thursday, local bank buying of U.S. dollars, suspected to be acting at the behest of the MAS, drove the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to an intraday high of S$1.6927 - lifting it off six-month lows. \par \par \uc2  Market observers said, however, that strength in the yen and euro, as well as robust domestic macroeconomic figures, will continue to put upward pressure on the Singapore dollar. \par \par \uc2  An economist at a U.K. bank said the MAS will be hard-pressed to maintain the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at current levels if the euro and yen stay strong. \par \par \uc2  He said he sees the U.S. dollar testing support of S$1.6700 next week if the trend continues. \par \par \uc2  On the local money market, the interbank overnight rate was offered at 1.750%, up from 1.500% late Wednesday in Asia, while the three-month rate was offered at 2.1875%, unchanged from late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  -By Anita Jain; 65-421-4807; anita.jain@dowjones.comtagline \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 29-07-99 \par \par \uc2  0907GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv7t05njb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
