\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  -2: Won, Singapore Dlr Both Pushed Down \b0\par\par\uc2 316 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juli 1999\par 10:44\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Korea Thursday forecast that exports would rise by 7% in the second half on a year-on-year basis, bringing the overall increase in export volume for 1999 to 3%. \par \par \uc2  The good economic news failed to buoy the won, however, as local banks continued to buy U.S. dollars in order to meet government requirements on loss provisioning for foreign assets. \par \par \uc2  The early provisioning requirement is just one of a number of measures introduced by the government in recent months to preserve Korea's export competitiveness by countering the trade and capital inflows pushing the won higher. \par \par \uc2  By the end of local dealing, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been pushed higher, to close at 1,203.50 won, up from KRW1,198.70 at the previous close. \par \par \uc2  Positive sentiment also failed to lift the Singapore dollar. After rising strongly in early Asian trading, with the U.S. dollar dropping to a fresh six-month low at S$1.6750, the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was pushed sharply lower by aggressive U.S. dollar buying from Singapore banks. \par \par \uc2  Most dealers assumed that the purchases were executed on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore, as the buying pushed the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  right up to levels above S$1.6900. \par \par \uc2  U.S. dollar sellers emerged at the high, however, and the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  settled back to S$1.6857 toward the end of Asian trading, up from S$1.6810 at the same time the day before. \par \par \uc2  Despite the suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , many dealers remain relatively positive on the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , reasoning that with the yen, the euro and other Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  relatively strong, the MAS should allow the Singapore dollar to appreciate against the dollar, in order to maintain a neutral trade-weighted exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 29-07-99 \par \par \uc2  0844GMT \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv7t05net\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
