\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Lifted By Yen, Easing Regional Concerns \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tom Holland \par \uc2 254 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juli 1999\par 10:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  - \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--A combination of the yen's strength, abating concern over the tensions between China and Taiwan, relief at South Korea's handling of the Daewoo Group's near collapse, and improving economic fundamentals lifted Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht, the Indonesian rupiah and the New Taiwan dollar all finished Asian trading hours higher. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar, however, ended down following suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The South Korean won closed lower, in response to government-directed dollar purchases by local banks. \par \par \uc2  But overall sentiment toward the region has improved markedly since a week ago, when withdrawal of funds by foreign investors spooked by the cross-strait squabble and Daewoo's cash crisis forced many Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to multiple-month lows. \par \par \uc2  "On the whole, the economic recovery is very much intact," explained Thio Chin Loo, global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Banque Paribas in Singapore, saying investors had been greatly reassured by unexpectedly strong industrial production numbers released this week by both South Korea and Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "There are very strong reasons why Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  should strengthen further from these levels," she said. \par \par \uc2  In South Korea, the government announced that industrial output surged by 29.5% year-on-year in June, the biggest rise in over 10 years. Coming on top of a 21.7% increase in May, the rise was attributed to a combination of rising export volume and resurgent domestic demand. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 29-07-99 \par \par \uc2  0830GMT \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv7t05nbg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
