\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2 : US Dlr Dragged Lower By Tumble Vs Yen \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tom Holland \par \uc2 247 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juli 1999\par 10:28\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  - \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The dollar's tumble against the yen dragged the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower against Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  during local trading hours Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  In southeast Asia, the dollar weakened against the Singapore dollar and dropped sharply against the Indonesian rupiah. Heavy sales of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  were also seen against the Thai baht, despite the closure of markets in Bangkok for a holiday. \par \par \uc2  In North Asian markets, the dollar dropped steadily from its opening high against the Korean won, slipping once again below the KRW1,200 level. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also softened against the new Taiwan dollar and the Philippine peso. \par \par \uc2  Further unwinding of Asian cross \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trades funded through short positions in the Singapore dollar was credited with driving much of the run-up in the Singapore dollar. \par \par \uc2  Although the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to surpass the six-month high it touched briefly Tuesday, traders generally expected it to push higher in coming sessions. \par \par \uc2  "The U.S. dollar's trend is still down," said one trader at a Singapore bank. \par \par \uc2  Given the weakness of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the yen, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively to support the U.S. dollar, he said, adding that the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could easily slide all the way to S$1.6700 over the short term. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 28-07-99 \par \par \uc2  0828GMT \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv7s05nx1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
