\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA MARKETS-Strong yen supports Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2      By Richard Hubbard \par \uc2 987 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juli 1999\par 11:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      HONG KONG, July 28 (Reuters) - The strength of the yen \par \par \uc2  underpinned the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on Monday sending the \par \par \uc2  regionals all slightly higher. \par \par \uc2      While most stock markets took their cue from the higher Wall \par \par \uc2  Street finish overnight to resume recent rallies, lead by Korean \par \par \uc2  investors who seem to have shaken off their Daewoo jitters. \par \par \uc2      BULLS RETURN TO KOREAN ASSET MARKETS \par \par \uc2      Early demand for the Korean won saw the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  break \par \par \uc2  through the 1200 level to the dollar drawing verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  from the authorities. \par \par \uc2      Korean finance ministry officials said they were closely \par \par \uc2  monitoring the market, and state banks were seen active buyers of \par \par \uc2  dollars. \par \par \uc2      In addition to the yen the won is getting a boost from signs \par \par \uc2  the Daewoo crisis might be moving toward a better outcome after \par \par \uc2  the creditors stepped in yesterday to take control of the \par \par \uc2  restructuring process. \par \par \uc2      Korea's KOSPI ended up around 1.7 percent after being as much \par \par \uc2  as four percent higher during the day.  But analysts doubt all \par \par \uc2  the bad news is out yet for the Korean corporate sector. \par \par \uc2      "Is Daewoo the only case in Korea where you have a severe \par \par \uc2  need for restructuring? I don't think so," said Andrew Dermot \par \par \uc2  Fung, regional treasury economist at Standard Chartered Bank in \par \par \uc2  Singapore. \par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE DOLLAR STRENGTHENS AS ECONOMIC OUTLOOK IMPROVES \par \par \uc2      The Singapore dollar pushed through the 1.69 level overnight \par \par \uc2  to a low of 1.6815 in the Asian day. \par \par \uc2      There were rumours of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market by the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities, though the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  does have a tendency \par \par \uc2  to track the yen. \par \par \uc2      But analysts and the authorities point out that the economy \par \par \uc2  is improving sharply as well. \par \par \uc2      Singapore's economy enjoyed better-than-expected growth in \par \par \uc2  the second quarter of 1999 and an upward revision in full-year \par \par \uc2  growth can be expected, the nation's deputy prime minister and \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief said. \par \par \uc2  "The second quarter has turned out better than we had \par \par \uc2  expected," Deputy Prime Minister Lee Hsien Loong told Reuters \par \par \uc2  Television in an interview. \par \par \uc2  GDP for 1999 is currently forecast up or down one percent on \par \par \uc2  last year. The Singapore government is expected to announce a new \par \par \uc2  forecast on National Day, August 9. \par \par \uc2  Singapore's total manufacturing output surged 18.4 percent \par \par \uc2  during the 12 months to June, the Economic Development Board said \par \par \uc2  on Monday. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIA LOOKS FOR STRONGER RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere Indonesia's economics minister Ginandjar, in Paris \par \par \uc2  for the Consultative Group meeting of international donors, was \par \par \uc2  again talking up the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  He said the government is comfortable with a dollar-rupiah \par \par \uc2  level around 6,500 and sees improvement to around 6,000 as a good \par \par \uc2  move. \par \par \uc2      However, Ginandjar hastened to add there would be no \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support such a move. \par \par \uc2      ASIA NEEDS TO BOOST DEMAND - WORLD BANK \par \par \uc2      Asia must focus on the restoration of demand and although it \par \par \uc2  is clear the crisis has bottomed out, the region is far from full \par \par \uc2  recovery, according to World Bank chief economist Joseph \par \par \uc2  Stiglitz. \par \par \uc2      "The real focus ought to be on the restoration of aggregate \par \par \uc2  demand in these countries," he told Reuters Television. \par \par \uc2      "While exchange rates have stabilised and clearly the crisis \par \par \uc2  has bottomed out, most of the countries are nowhere near recovery \par \par \uc2  in terms of fundamentals of output, employment and real wages." \par \par \uc2      He said there was still a lot of room for stimulating demand. \par \par \uc2      Stiglitz indicated he favoured a continuation of relaxed \par \par \uc2  monetary policy in the crisis countries, although he said there \par \par \uc2  was room in those recovering more quickly to bear higher rates. \par \par \uc2      "In general for the region as a whole the fact is the \par \par \uc2  recovery is nowhere along so far that one can be complacent." \par \par \uc2      REGIONAL STOCKS ALL RALLY \par \par \uc2      The Dow's strong one percent gain overnight set the stage for \par \par \uc2  a good day around the region. \par \par \uc2      In Singapore the Straits Times index shot up by 3.6 percent, \par \par \uc2  boosted by some strong results from DBS Land on Tuesday. The \par \par \uc2  company unveiled a 174 percent rise in interim profits. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par \uc2   Change on the day WED 28 0852GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...Latest bid....Prev Close....Pct Move \par