\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dollar Stronger Late;  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 326 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juli 1999\par 12:31\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar strengthened against the U.S. dollar late Tuesday, but has fallen off a six-month high on suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At 0950 GMT (5:50 a.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.6880, weaker than S$1.6973 late Monday, but higher than its intraday low of S$1.6797. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS) is believed to have bought U.S. dollars Tuesday through local banks to arrest the Singapore dollar's rapid climb. \par \par \uc2  The authority rarely comments on its daily activities, but admits to controlling large movements in the market. \par \par \uc2  Before the MAS reportedly stepped in, stop-loss orders triggered at the S$1.6850 level carried the U.S. dollar through support at S$1.6800, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They also noted an MAS report that said \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flows in and out of a country shouldn't be regulated had suggested to market players that the de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was easing its grip on the market, imbuing participants with confidence in pushing the Singapore dollar higher without being caught short U.S. dollars by an MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar's steep descent against the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar began late Monday, following both the yen's sharp rise and the bullish industrial production figures for Singapore showing June total manufacturing output rose 18.4%. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at a U.S. bank said the positive figures point to strong economic growth, which will put pressure on the MAS to yield on its monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  On the local money market, the interbank overnight rate was offered at 1.250%, down from 1.625% late Monday in Asia, while the three-month rate was offered at 2.1875%, down from 2.3750% late Monday. \par \par \uc2  -By Anita Jain; 65-421-4807; anita.jain@dowjones.comtagline \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 27-07-99 \par \par \uc2  1031GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv7r05kuy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
