\par\par \b \uc2  EMERGING MARKET  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 - \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  in thrall to Fed. \b0\par\par\uc2 635 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juli 1999\par 12:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      LONDON, July 27 (Reuters) - Emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  recovered slightly on Tuesday after Monday's losses, but were \par \par \uc2  still held in thrall by the second part of Federal Reserve \par \par \uc2  Chairman Alan Greenspan's Humphrey-Hawkins testimony on \par \par \uc2  Wednesday, analysts said. \par \par \uc2      However, Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  saw a recovery as a result of \par \par \uc2  gains on the region's stock markets, with the Korean won firmer \par \par \uc2  after creditors stepped in to take over the restructuring of the \par \par \uc2  ailing Daewoo conglomerate, said Callum Henderson, emerging \par \par \uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Citibank. \par \par \uc2      The Korean won firmed to 1203 bid to the dollar, up from \par \par \uc2  1208 in early London trade on Monday. \par \par \uc2      But it is Greenspan who holds sway. \par \par \uc2      "Overall the environment remains pretty jittery," said \par \par \uc2  Henderson. "Since the U.S. is basically the provider of global \par \par \uc2  liquidity, that automatically weighs on emerging markets." \par \par \uc2      East Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  benefited from some strength in the \par \par \uc2  Singapore dollar, which posted sharp gains on Monday. \par \par \uc2      Some analysts said they suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities had \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      The Taiwan dollar was aided by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \par \par \uc2  Monday and closed unchanged on Tuesday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading \par \par \uc2  at 32.230 in London. \par \par \uc2      Standard Chartered said in a note to investors that the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  looked capped at 32.30 and an "apparent easing of \par \par \uc2  tension with China, combined with injections of funds, is \par \par \uc2  resulting in interest rates adopting a marginally softer bias". \par \par \uc2      Stanchart believes that some of the bearishness on emerging \par \par \uc2  market assets as a result of the Fed testimony has gone too far. \par \par \uc2      "However, as concerns about the Fed appear overdone, \par \par \uc2  pessimism about regional markets appears to be exaggerated," the \par \par \uc2  bank said. \par \par \uc2      In eastern Europe, the picture was somewhat similar to Asia, \par \par \uc2  with \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  posting some gains after the Fed-inspired \par \par \uc2  selloff in global markets on Monday. \par \par \uc2      The Polish zloty opened at 6.10 percent above parity against \par \par \uc2  its basket of euros and dollars and was trading a tad weaker \par \par \uc2  than its domestic opening price of 4.0516 to the euro and was at \par \par \uc2  4.0591 bid to the euro by 1000 GMT. \par \par \uc2  "As recent comments about a higher current account deficit \par \par \uc2  are still being digested, we expect the zloty to stabilise \par \par \uc2  around the six percent level," said Mark Rall, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  strategist at HypoVeriensbank. \par \par \uc2      Rall expects the Czech crown to appreciate to around 36.50 \par \par \uc2  to the euro in coming days from 36.669 now. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab \tab     LATEST  PREV    P