\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Up Late; Mkt Unwinds Long US Dlr Positions \b0\par\par\uc2 224 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juli 1999\par 11:39\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar has strengthened against the U.S. dollar late Tuesday as market players unwind their long U.S. dollar positions on the apparent easing of tensions between China and Taiwan, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0845 GMT (4:45 a.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.6972, down from S$1.7052 late Monday in Asia and from S$1.6995 earlier Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at a European bank said traders who had gone long the U.S. dollar last week as friction between China and Taiwan intensified were now adjusting their positions. \par \par \uc2  "There's a lot of unwinding of cross-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hedges put on last Friday," he said. \par \par \uc2  He said that although there is momentum to push the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar stronger against the U.S. dollar, fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to keep it from strengthening above S$1.6950 against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  On the local money market, the interbank overnight rate was offered at 1.125%, down from 2.250% late Monday in Asia, while the three-month rate was offered at 1.875%, down from 2.125% late Monday. \par \par \uc2  -By Anita Jain; 65-421-4807 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 20-07-99 \par \par \uc2  0939GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv7k05bnp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
