\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Slightly Weaker Early;Moving In Tight Range \b0\par\par\uc2 239 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juli 1999\par 04:23\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar is slightly weaker early Tuesday against the U.S. dollar after moving in a very narrow range overnight. \par \par \uc2  At 0140 GMT (9:40 p.m. Monday EDT), the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.6995, higher than its level of S$1.6980 in late Monday trade in Asia. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said trade in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been sluggish following the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market last week. \par \par \uc2  "There's been no incentive to trade after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a dealer at a Japanese bank said. \par \par \uc2  He said that while traders are wary of taking the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar higher on fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , commercial selling of the U.S. dollar above S$1.7000 is keeping trade mired in a tight range. \par \par \uc2  "Corporate demand (for the Singapore dollar) is capping the upside of the (U.S.) dollar," he said. \par \par \uc2  The dealer said the U.S. dollar is likely to track a course between S$1.6850 and S$1.7250 for the rest of the month. \par \par \uc2  On the local money market, the interbank overnight rate was offered at 2.000%, down from 2.125% late Monday in Asia, while the three-month rate was offered at 1.9375%, up from 1.875% late Monday. \par \par \uc2  -By Anita Jain; 421-4807 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 13-07-99 \par \par \uc2  0223GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv