\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  -3: NT Dlr Strengthens To 5-Mo High \b0\par\par\uc2 341 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juli 1999\par 11:27\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar, too, edged higher Monday. But following the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market last week to arrest the appreciation of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , market players were tentative buyers. \par \par \uc2  Late in Asian trading, the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.6980, down from S$1.7000 at the same time Friday. \par \par \uc2  Although there is interest from investment funds to sell the U.S. dollar at S$1.7000, bids at S$1.6950 from local banks and speculative players should support the market in the short term, said dealers. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah ended up slightly on the day, but with few investors willing to risk taking fresh positions in the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  while the political situation remains up in the air, the U.S. dollar is unlikely to fall below bids at the IDR6,610 level, said traders. \par \par \uc2  Late in Asian trading the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at IDR6,637, down from IDR6,685 Friday. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the New Taiwan dollar lifted in line with other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to close at a five-month high against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  Despite near-daily \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to check the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise, the New Taiwan dollar is set to appreciate further over the medium term, according to analysts at Standard Chartered Bank. \par \par \uc2  In a research note issued Monday afternoon they said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of China, Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has little option but to sanction a mild appreciation of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The bank's tactics of sterilizing its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by issuing bonds to soak up domestic liquidity "simply attracts more inflows due to the upward pressure on local rates and enhanced appreciation expectations resulting from rising reserves." \par \par \uc2  At the close of local trading Monday, the U.S. dollar was quoted at NT$32.255, down from NT$32.283 Friday. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 852 2832 2341; tom.holland@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 12-07-99 \par \par \uc2  0927GMT \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv7c056gl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
