\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar Slightly Stronger Early;Players Cautious \b0\par\par\uc2 229 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juli 1999\par 04:16\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar is slightly stronger against the U.S. dollar early Friday on some commercial demand, but trade is expected to remain range-bound, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  About 0140 GMT (9:40 p.m. Thursday EDT), the U.S. dollar was trading at S$1.6982, down from S$1.7000 in late Thursday trade and its overnight high of S$1.7015. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said market players are still wary of pushing up the Singapore dollar too much following the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market earlier this week. \par \par \uc2  They noted that the de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's admission of its action in the market sends a clear signal that it is vigilant about the Singapore dollar's movements, and will act to suppress excessive strength which would erode export competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at a Japanese brokerage said given the caution in the market, the Singapore dollar is likely to trade in a very narrow range Friday. \par \par \uc2  On the local money market, the interbank overnight rate was offered at 2.000%, up from 1.875% late Thursday in Asia, while the three-month rate was offered at 1.8125%, unchanged from late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  -By Anita Jain; 65-421-4807; anita.jain@cor.dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 09-07-99 \par \par \uc2  0216GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv79055ma\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\pic