\par\par \b \uc2  EMERGING MARKET  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Sentiment turns slightly worse. \b0\par\par\uc2 538 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juli 1999\par 11:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      LONDON, July 9 (Reuters) - Emerging market \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were weaker on Friday as recent bullish \par \par \uc2  sentiment turned moderately negative after a statement \par \par \uc2  that Argentine tax revenues in July are expected to be \par \par \uc2  10 percent lower than a year earlier. \par \par \uc2      Trade was subdued and Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were weaker, \par \par \uc2  with even the Polish zloty stalled in its march to new \par \par \uc2  highs, traders and analysts said. \par \par \uc2      Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are expected to resume their upward \par \par \uc2  march as fund managers increase allocations to the \par \par \uc2  region and economic growth sucks in foreign direct \par \par \uc2  investment. \par \par \uc2      "However, even with dollar/yen seemingly well \par \par \uc2  supported by the threat of repeated Bank of Japan \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  to similarly support dollar/Singapore \par \par \uc2  dollar, this is seen as a relatively short-lived \par \par \uc2  phenomenon," said Standard Chartered strategist Mitul \par \par \uc2  Kotecha. \par \par \uc2      The Korean won was again weaker. It has fallen some \par \par \uc2  30 won against the U.S. dollar in the past week and by \par \par \uc2  0810 GMT was trading at 1186.9 bid. \par \par \uc2      StanChart said that if the won breaks 1190 to the \par \par \uc2  dollar, the next support is at 1205. \par \par \uc2      "Short-term prospects are relatively firm though \par \par \uc2  exporter selling may slow the rate of gain," the bank \par \par \uc2  said. \par \par \uc2      In central Europe, both the zloty and the Czech \par \par \uc2  crown saw their rises halt. \par \par \uc2      The zloty started Thursday in the same bullish mood \par \par \uc2  which has characterised its recent performance. However \par \par \uc2  a move above six percent above parity against its basket \par \par \uc2  of dollars and euros failed to hold, and it moved back \par \par \uc2  to 5.7 percent above parity by the close. \par \par \uc2      The zloty opened weaker on Friday at 3.9785 bid to \par \par \uc2  the euro and 3.9090 bid against the dollar. \par \par \uc2      "The zloty should trade between 5.4 percent and 5.7 \par \par \uc2  percent on the strong side of parity," said \par \par \uc2  HypoVeriensbank strategist Stefan Kolek. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab \tab    LATEST   PREV   PCT CHG PCT CHG\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab      ON YEAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par EUROPE/MEAST/AFRICA\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Czech Rep.\tab \tab     36.31   36.21   0.27%   4.33%\par Poland\tab \tab \tab   3.98    3.98    0.05%   -2.20%\par Hungary\tab \tab \tab  248.94  249.07  -0.05%  -0.90%\par Slovakia\tab \tab \tab 45.23   45.28   -0.11%  5.18%\par Romania\tab \tab \tab  15,835  15,850  -0.09%  44.61%\par Ukraine\tab \tab \tab  3.96    3.96    -0.03%  0.81%\par South Africa\tab \tab   6.08    6.06    0.33%   4.05%\par Kenya\tab \tab \tab    72.15   72.15   0.00%   17.13%\par Israel\tab \tab \tab   4.093   4.078   0.38%   -0.63%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par LATAM\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Mexico\tab \tab \tab   9.35    9.34    0.05%   -5.03%\par Brazil\tab \tab \tab   1.8010  1.8010  0.00%   49.20%\par Venezuela\tab \tab      608.50  608.50  0.00%   7.79%\par Chile\tab \tab \tab    5