\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  -3: Position-Squaring Saps Baht, Peso \b0\par\par\uc2 270 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juli 1999\par 11:57\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Purchases of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the baht by U.S. and European banks that went short the U.S. dollar last week were blamed for depressing the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to its lowest level since early June. \par \par \uc2  The banks moved to exit their trades after the U.S. dollar held firm above Y122 and after Wednesday's admission by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  that it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar. \par \par \uc2  "They saw the baht wasn't going to go very far and so they covered their positions, pushing the dollar higher," explained the head trader at a Thai bank. \par \par \uc2  Late in Asian trading, the U.S. dollar was quoted at 37.0400 baht, up from THB36.8850 the day before. With dollar selling interest seen emerging from Bangkok at the dollar's highs for the day, dealers said the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would struggle to climb above THB37.10 in the near term. \par \par \uc2  Continued position-squaring was also behind the weakening of the Philippine peso, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dropped to its lowest level since early April. \par \par \uc2  Traders said foreign investors who had bought the peso for its high yield have exited their positions as successive interest-rate cuts in the Philippines and last week's U.S. interest-rate hike have narrowed the positive carry available on the peso. \par \par \uc2  At the close of local trading Thursday, the U.S. dollar was quoted at 38.440 pesos, up from PHP38.300 the day before. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 08-07-99 \par \par \uc2  0957GMT \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv7805450\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
