\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Lower Late In Line With US Dlr Bullishness \b0\par\par\uc2 249 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juli 1999\par 11:07\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar fell against the U.S. dollar in late trading Thursday, dragged down by the Thai baht's slide against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  At 0830 GMT (4:30 a.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar was trading around S$1.7000, up from S$1.6960 in late Wednesday trade in Asia and from S$1.6987 earlier Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar is quoted at 37.03 baht, up from THB36.955 at the close of trading Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at a U.S. bank said U.S. funds were buying into the U.S. dollar on a short-term basis in sympathy with the dollar's bullish turn against regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers, however, noted strong selling resistance for the U.S. dollar at S$1.7010-S$1.7020, in line with Singapore's faster-than-expected recovery from the regional crisis. \par \par \uc2  Dealers noted that market participants, spooked by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's acknowledged \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets late Tuesday, are reluctant to push the Singapore dollar up too high. \par \par \uc2  On the local money market, the interbank overnight rate was offered at 1.875%, up from 1.750% late Wednesday in Asia, while the three-month rate was offered at 1.8125%, unchanged from late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  -By Anita Jain; 65-421-4807; anita.jain@cor.dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 08-07-99 \par \par \uc2  0907GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv78053yq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\s