\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar Lower Early On Weaker Yen, Stk Mkt \b0\par\par\uc2 334 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juli 1999\par 04:10\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar has weakened a touch against the U.S. dollar early Thursday from its levels late Wednesday as the yen's weakness and the Singapore stock market helped give the U.S. dollar a lift, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  About 0145 GMT (9:45 p.m. EDT Wednesday), the U.S. dollar was trading at S$1.6987, up from S$1.6960 in late Wednesday trade in Asia. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar-yen is firmly above Y122 and this is exerting some influence" on the Singapore dollar a dealer at a U.S. bank said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is trading at Y122.30, above Y122.22 in New York late Wednesday, and also up from Y122.14 late Wednesday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Singapore's benchmark Straits Times Index tumbled 1.4% Wednesday, correcting from a rally last week that had pushed shares to their all-time highs. \par \par \uc2  Stock market bullishness had lent support to the local dollar, and so its retreat helped drag it down, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market is also still smarting from the acknowledged \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which stepped into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets late Tuesday to quell excessive Singapore dollar strength. \par \par \uc2  "The market was caught very long on Singapore dollars," the dealer at a U.S. bank said. "There's some position adjusting." \par \par \uc2  He said that although these factors were conspiring to weaken the Singapore dollar Thursday, the medium-term outlook is for a bullish Singapore dollar. \par \par \uc2  The dealer said that a break for the U.S. dollar below S$1.6850 would pave the way for a steeper move to S$1.6500. \par \par \uc2  On the local money market, the interbank overnight rate was offered at 1.750%, unchanged from late Wednesday in Asia, while the three-month rate also remained unchanged at 1.8125%. \par \par \uc2  -By Anita Jain; 65-421-4807; anita.jain@cor.dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 08-07-99 \par \par \uc2  0210GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv780532e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
