\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Open Lower Vs Dlr In Subdued Trading \b0\par\par\uc2 288 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juli 1999\par 03:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have opened a fraction lower against the U.S. dollar in Asian trading Thursday, but brokers describe trading interest as extremely limited. \par \par \uc2  "The market is dead this morning," said one Singapore-based \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  broker. \par \par \uc2  'It's very quiet. I think these markets are going to be pretty rangy today," added another. \par \par \uc2  At 0045 GMT (8:45 p.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar is quoted against the Singapore dollar at S$1.6975, little changed from S$1.6970 late in Asia the previous day. \par \par \uc2  Following a rare confirmation from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  that it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market by buying U.S. dollars late Tuesday, dealers are extremely reluctant to assume fresh positions. \par \par \uc2  Against the Thai baht (THB), the U.S. dollar is quoted at THB36.9300 up from THB36.8850 late the day before. \par \par \uc2  With the dollar approaching the top of recent THB36.75 to THB36.95 range, brokers say selling interest is emerging at levels above THB36.92, which should restrict further gains by the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Against the Indonesian rupiah (IDR), the U.S. dollar is at IDR6,735 compared with IDR6,770 late the day before. \par \par \uc2  Against the South Korean won (KRW), the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has opened at KRW1,176.50, up sharply from KRW1,173.00 at the previous close. \par \par \uc2  Trading in the Philippine peso (PHP) and the new Taiwan dollar has yet to begin. At Wednesday's close the U.S. dollar was at PHP38.300 and NT$32.285. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 852 2832 2341; tom.holland@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 08-07-99 \par \par \uc2  0100GMT \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv78052xf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
