\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  ease, KOSPI breaches 1,000. \b0\par\par\uc2 927 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juli 1999\par 11:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, July 7 (Reuters) - Most Asian markets were in a \par \par \uc2  consolidation mode on Wednesday, as \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  finished \par \par \uc2  slightly weaker and stocks wilted toward the end of trade. \par \par \uc2      KOSPI ENDS ABOVE 1,000, FIRST IN NEARLY FOUR YEARS \par \par \uc2      But South Korea's KOSPI went against the region's easier \par \par \uc2  trend, closing above 1,000 points for the first time in 45 \par \par \uc2  months. \par \par \uc2      Brokers said retail fund buying prompted institutions to \par \par \uc2  load up on stocks. \par \par \uc2      Analysts said it could take some time before the index \par \par \uc2  settles comfortably above 1,000. Some expect it to consolidate \par \par \uc2  before firming further. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it expected the economy to grow an \par \par \uc2  average 6.8 percent year-on-year in 1999 and 7.2 percent in the \par \par \uc2  second half. \par \par \uc2      The outlook was even more bullish than the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of\b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Economy's recent forecast of five to six percent \par \par \uc2  growth year-on-year for both periods. \par \par \uc2      "If (Koreans) continually revise their growth figures, \par \par \uc2  they're also going to have to expect to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  more \par \par \uc2  frequently in the market as people become more bullish about \par \par \uc2  the economy," said Andrew Dermot-Fung, treasury economist at \par \par \uc2  Standard Chartered. \par \par \uc2  The won extended its losses as interbank operators bought \par \par \uc2  dollars to meet new \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  loan-loss provisioning \par \par \uc2  rules. \par \par \uc2  The government has directed local banks to complete \par \par \uc2  building up the provisions by the end of September, three \par \par \uc2  months earlier than scheduled. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  DOLLAR WEAKER, WARY OF \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar was still weaker after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday to curb its rise. \par \par \uc2  In its annual report on the economy the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said \par \par \uc2  prospects for the second half of the year onwards were good, \par \par \uc2  but also warned it was too early to conclude it was "totally \par \par \uc2  out of the woods." \par \par \uc2      "Major uncertainties lie ahead," said an official in the \par \par \uc2  annual report. \par \par \uc2      The comment followed an earlier statement by the deputy \par \par \uc2  prime minister that the government would make an upward \par \par \uc2  revision to its 1999 GDP growth forecast, since the economy was \par \par \uc2  growing faster than expected. \par \par \uc2  Standard Chartered's Dermot-Fung said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore was doing well in taking a cautious \par \par \uc2  stance on economic outlook. \par \par \uc2  "One of the things that we are seeing in regional equity \par \par \uc2  markets is that retail investors are being very optimistic," he \par \par \uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  "It seems to reflect a view that once the recovery is in \par \par \uc2  place, we will get back to very strong growth levels. And \par \par \uc2  clearly that is not going to be the case and I think MAS is \par \par \uc2  actually doing well by trying to tone down people's expectatons \par \par \uc2  of what the economy will look like in the post-crisis era." \par \par \uc2  Singapore shares fell although brokers said there was no \par \par \uc2  specific news that could have led to the fall, except for \par \par \uc2  on-going talk of credit curbs on retail punters. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN TRADE FIGURES BOOST SHARES \par \par \uc2  Stronger than expected June trade figures lifted Taiwan \par \par \uc2  stocks, wiping out early losses on recent credit-tightening \par \par \uc2  moves. The index closed 0.18 percent higher at 8,470.07. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan's June exports were up 8.2 percent year-on-year, and \par \par \uc2  imports were a solid 5.2 percent higher after several months of \par \par \uc2  flat of negative year-on-year change. \par \par \uc2      Both figures exceeded market expectations, giving off \par \par \uc2  strong signs of recovery. \par \par \uc2      THAI FINANCIAL SHARES PULL DOWN INDEX \par \par \uc2      Thailand's stock index weakened as downward momentum and \par \par \uc2  worries about the financial sector induced more selling. \par \par \uc2      Brokers said rumours that the government may close down \par \par \uc2  more ailing finance companies were used as an excuse to take \par \par \uc2  profits from recent gains in the financial sector. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  Change on the day WED 07 0825GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...Latest bid....Prev Close....Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7998.......3.8000.........0.01% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......6740.00......6707.00........-0.49% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........36.87........36.77........-0.27% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........38.27........38.12........-0.39% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.6960.......1.6900........-0.35% \par \