\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-S'pore MAS narrows  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  band,upbeat on economy. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Valerie Lee \par \uc2 650 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juli 1999\par 10:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, July 7 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS) said economic prospects were positive for the second half of 1999 and beyond, adding it would revert to a pre-crisis \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate policy band as regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility had died down. \par \par \uc2  "Prospects for a sustained economic recovery into the second half of 1999 and beyond are good," MAS managing director Koh Yong Guan said at the release of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's annual report on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "The external environment is expected to be favourable and the policy measures taken in 1998 in response to the economic slowdown are beginning to take effect," he said. \par \par \uc2  The typically conservative \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  warned, however, that Singapore's economy was not totally "out of the woods" as major uncertainties lay ahead. \par \par \uc2  "There are risk factors to watch out for, particularly a sharp correction in the U.S. stock market, a weakening of the Japanese yen, and rising protectionist pressures," Koh said in the report. \par \par \uc2  Koh declined to peg any levels for Singapore's gross domestic product (GDP) growth rate for the year, but said economic data indicated that a revision of government forecasts slated for August would likely be a change "on the upside". \par \par \uc2  Singapore Deputy Prime Minister Lee Hsien Loong, also chairman of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said in parliament on Tuesday that the economy was recovering faster than expected and the government would revise the growth forecast in August, when full economic results for the second quarter became available. \par \par \uc2  The government's 1999 GDP forecast currently sees growth of between zero to two percent, but some economists told Reuters the actual figure could be as high as four percent for the year. \par \par \uc2  Koh added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which broadened the trading band for the Singapore dollar last year in response to the Asian financial crisis, would return the band to the pre-crisis width. \par \par \uc2  He said the move was not an indication by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that it would tolerate a stronger Singapore dollar but was more in response to the stabilising of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  "The widening of the band last year did allow for a greater appreciation of the Singapore dollar than would otherwise have been the case..., conversely it cannot be that narrowing of the band is aimed at the strengthening of the Singapore dollar," said MAS Deputy Managing Director Tharman Shanmugaratnam. \par \par \uc2  Singapore does not publish information about the band. \par \par \uc2  MAS officials, traditionally tight-lipped about the bank's action in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, confirmed on Wednesday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had stepped into the market on Tuesday to dampen a surge in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against its U.S. counterpart. \par \par \uc2  "Just as we \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the downside last year when people were unduly pessimistic, so too we have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the upside," said Yeo Lian Sim, MAS assistant managing director of capital markets. \par \par \uc2  At 0705 GMT on Wednesday, the Singapore dollar was trading at 1.6967/77 to the U.S. unit. It reached a high of 1.6870 in thin overnight trading, a high not seen since mid-April. \par \par \uc2  Koh said MAS was maintaining its current neutral exchange rate policy stance as the Singapore economy was "still operating below potential" and the inflation outlook was benign. \par \par \uc2  "At the moment the economy is recovering nicely so we have set a neutral policy path," said Khor Hoe Ee, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's senior executive director, economics. \par \par \uc2  "But once the economy has recovered fully and it seems to be overheating then we of course have to react, but we don't see that as a risk at the moment." \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had said in its report that overall consumer price index inflation was expected to be zero percent in 1999. \par \par \uc2  ((Singapore newsroom (65) 8703080 fax: (65) 7768112 singapore.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7704xux\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
