\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dlr Dn Late After Tue  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 , Quiet Wed \b0\par\par\uc2 395 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juli 1999\par 11:39\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is lower late Wednesday compared with a day earlier, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  during Tuesday's European session, then admitted the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  About 0920 GMT (5:20 a.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar was trading at S$1.6960, up from S$1.6880 late Tuesday in Asia just ahead of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but down from its overnight peak of S$1.7005. \par \par \uc2  The rare admission Wednesday and the unusually late market action Tuesday kept the Singapore dollar in a tight trading range during Wednesday's Asian session. \par \par \uc2  The MAS, Singapore's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Wednesday it bought U.S. dollars Tuesday to stem excessive Singapore dollar strength. Yeo Liam Sim, MAS assistant managing director for capital markets, wouldn't reveal the size of the purchases, but said it was "sufficient" to serve its purpose. \par \par \uc2  "We \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and we consider that we did a good job yesterday," Yeo said. \par \par \uc2  Traders and analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  indicates the MAS is not likely to allow the U.S. dollar to fall below S$1.69, and was also a reaction to obvious speculative positions being built up. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  triggered short covering by players betting the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar would appreciate, especially as the economic outlook brightened. \par \par \uc2  Market participants are wary of testing the MAS resolve again, and the U.S. dollar is seen caught in a narrow range of about S$1.6960 to S$1.6990. \par \par \uc2  Adding to the sense of caution, the MAS also said Wednesday it was switching to a narrower exchange rate policy band, suggesting it would tolerate less fluctuation of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  when measured against a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  While the switch will still allow the Singapore dollar to shift in line with other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it could make the MAS quicker to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if it feels the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's moves aren't supported by fundamentals, watchers said. \par \par \uc2  On the local money market, the interbank overnight rate was offered at 1.750%, up from 0.875% late Tuesday in Asia, while the three-month rate was offered at 1.8125%, up from 1.6825% late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  -By Roger Malone; 65/421-4800; roger.malone@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 07-07-99 \par \par \uc2  0939GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv77054po\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
