\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  MAS  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Band Move May Spur More  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 444 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juli 1999\par 07:29\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--A decision by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore to narrow its acceptable trading band for the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar could trigger more frequent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts said. \par \par \uc2  But the announcement - which comes a day after the authority stepped into the market to punish speculators - also reflects increased market stability, which in turn may make \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  less necessary, they said. \par \par \uc2  During a press conference to release its annual report, MAS Managing Director Koh Yong Guan said the authority has narrowed its exchange rate policy band to a width it carried before the regional economic crisis erupted. \par \par \uc2  He also said the authority would maintain its neutral stance toward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates. \par \par \uc2  Koh didn't give details about the policy band, but repeated a long-standing MAS policy that the authority manages the Singapore dollar against a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Last year, the MAS said it had widened the band in reaction to increased market volatility spurred by the regional crisis. \par \par \uc2  Analysts and traders said the policy shift means the authority will tolerate less fluctuation by the Singapore dollar on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, although it still allows the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to move generally in line with regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thio Chin Loo, Asia strategist for Banque Paribas in Singapore, said\par the announcement signals the MAS is comfortable with the internal and\par external economic environment.\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Followed Unwarranted Move On \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Mkt\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Also, with inflation expected to be flat this year, there's no need\par for an aggressive strengthening of the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , she said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "There is no need for the Singapore dollar to fluctuate as much as is\par has in the past," she said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A senior trader at an Asian bank in Singapore agreed, adding,\par "essentially, they don't like to see the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar speculated\par against."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Market watchers said Tuesday's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which was confirmed\par Wednesday by the MAS came in reaction to obvious speculative positions\par that pushed the Singapore dollar higher.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The U.S. dollar dipped as low as S$1.6880 late Tuesday before it was\par boosted by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and short covering to as high as S$1.7010.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par About 0445 GMT (12:45 a.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar was trading at\par S$1.6982.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Yeo Liam Sim, MAS assistant managing director for capital markets,\par said the authority bought U.S. dollars against the Singapore \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par halt excessive Singapore dollar strength.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The speed of the (Singapore dollar's) movement was going ahead of\par what the economy was doing," she said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Roger Malone; 65/421-4800; roger.malone@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 07-07-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0529GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1134 4190 55126 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv770543w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
