\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar Higher Early, Watching For MAS Action \b0\par\par\uc2 355 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juli 1999\par 03:42\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar is higher in early Asian trading Tuesday, but a sharp move is unlikely as the market remains wary of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  About 0100 GMT (9 p.m. Monday EDT), the U.S. dollar was trading at S$1.6940, down from S$1.6990 late Monday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  Continued economic optimism and a generally bullish stock market have given the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  an upward bias, but at these levels, traders are watching for signs that MAS will step in to cap the Singapore dollar's strength. \par \par \uc2  Traders also report foreign banks selling U.S. dollars in early Tuesday action, putting more upward pressure on the Singapore dollar. \par \par \uc2  "I think MAS will be in somewhere on the low side of S$1.69," a trader at an Asian bank in Singapore said. "It is probably the only country in the world that is trying to discourage people from taking up the stock market and strengthening the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  Although Singapore officials have repeatedly denied using the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a trade tool, the market believes MAS is working to keep the Singapore dollar from strengthening too much and eroding the country's export competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  Also, officials have stressed that while there are signs of recovery, the country is not yet in the clear, and belt-tighening measures taken to counter last year's recession must stay in place. \par \par \uc2  Deputy Prime Minister Lee Hsien Loong repeated this message in a magazine interview released Tuesday in which he says the local stock rally has overstated the recovery. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar's strength is seen capped around S$1.6930 to the U.S. dollar Monday, while orders should hold any weakness to around S$1.6980, traders said. \par \par \uc2  On the local money market, the interbank overnight rate was offered at 1.625%, unchanged from late Tuesday in Asia, while the three-month rate was offered at 1.6875%, also unchanged. \par \par \uc2  -By Roger Malone; 65/421-4800; roger.malone@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 06-07-99 \par \par \uc2  0142GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv76051w4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
