\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Down Late, But Commercial Orders Cap Move \b0\par\par\uc2 299 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juli 1999\par 11:52\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--Commercial orders for Singapore dollars kept the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's losses to a minimum in the Asian session Monday despite a fall by the Japanese yen against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  About 0925 GMT (5:25 a.m. EDT), the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading at S$1.6990, up from S$1.6980 late Friday in Asia and from a low over the weekend of S$1.6965. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also moving at Y122.45, up from Y121.02 late Friday in New York. \par \par \uc2  Traders said yen weakness early in the day, brought on by Bank of Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, helped bring the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar down to nearly S$1.70 to the U.S. dollar as the week's session opened. \par \par \uc2  But commercial interest in selling U.S. dollars brought the move to a quick halt. \par \par \uc2  "There's no sign of local interest, and interbank players are very quiet," a trader at a U.S. bank in Singapore said. \par \par \uc2  Overall interest was light, partly because of a U.S. holiday Monday, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Corporate interest in selling U.S. dollars could give the Singapore dollar a strong tone for most of the week, but some players will be looking for a move by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore to buy U.S. dollars if the strength gets out of hand. \par \par \uc2  On the local money market, the interbank overnight rate was offered at 1.625%, down from 2.500% late Friday in Asia, while the three-month rate was offered at 1.6875%, down from 1.750% late Friday. \par \par \uc2  -By Roger Malone; 65/421-4800; roger.malone@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 05-07-99 \par \par \uc2  0952GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv75050bn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
