\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA MARKETS - Take Fed move in their stride. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Richard Hubbard \par \uc2 900 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juli 1999\par 12:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, July 2 (Reuters) - Asian markets welcomed on \par \par \uc2  Thursday the U.S. Fed's decision to implement a small rate hike \par \par \uc2  and move to a neutral stance on future policy, but their \par \par \uc2  attention was quickly focused on bullish domestic developments. \par \par \uc2      The Asian markets' reaction was also muted by holidays in \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong and Taiwan -- two of the most U.S. interest \par \par \uc2  rate-sensitive markets in Asia -- and in Thailand. \par \par \uc2      KOREA'S RECOVERY ACCELERATES, STOCKS CELEBRATE \par \par \uc2      South Korea outperformed the region once again, helped by the \par \par \uc2  U.S. interest rate move, positive economic news and a decision by \par \par \uc2  one of the big chaebol to seek receivership for an unprofitable \par \par \uc2  auto unit. \par \par \uc2      Seoul's KOSPI closed at a 37-month high of 919.98 points, up \par \par \uc2  4.19 percent on the day. \par \par \uc2      South Korea said it expected the economy to maintain healthy \par \par \uc2  growth of five to six percent year-on-year in the second half of \par \par \uc2  1999 and for the whole of 1999. \par \par \uc2      In its second-half policy review, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \par \par \uc2  Economy also forecast GDP would expand seven percent in the \par \par \uc2  second quarter after posting a 4.6 percent rise in the first \par \par \uc2  quarter. \par \par \uc2  The ministry predicted the country's consumer price index \par \par \uc2  (CPI) would rise about two percent year-on-year in 1999, against \par \par \uc2  7.5 percent the previous year. \par \par \uc2  "The CPI will rise more or less in the second half on the \par \par \uc2  back of the economic recovery, but for the year it is forecast to \par \par \uc2  stabilise at around two percent," the ministry said. \par \par \uc2  It also said South Korea's total external liabilities were \par \par \uc2  projected to fall below $139 billion by the end of 1999, after \par \par \uc2  payments on $10 billion to $14 billion worth of loans were made \par \par \uc2  during the year. \par \par \uc2  News that Samsung was willing to seek receivership for its \par \par \uc2  debt laden auto unit rather than sell it to the Daewoo Group was \par \par \uc2  also seen an encouraging sign of chaebol restructuring. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON SET TO STRENGTHEN \par \par \uc2  In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not sighted on \par \par \uc2  Thursday after Wednesday's buying of dollars, but analysts said \par \par \uc2  the positive economic number would see the won head higher. \par \par \uc2  "We could well see the Korean won breach the 1,150 level," \par \par \uc2  said Daniel Lian, Asian strategist at Barclays Capital in \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of Korea is already poised to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at this \par \par \uc2  level, and in the last three or four days they are able to \par \par \uc2  convince the market not to test the level. \par \par \uc2      "But I think further down the road we could see Korean won \par \par \uc2  trading below the 1,150 level," Lian said. \par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE SHARES ROCKET TO NEW HIGHS \par \par \uc2      Singapore's red-hot share market closed up 2.17 percent, at a \par \par \uc2  new record finish of 2,214.75, breaking through significant \par \par \uc2  resistance around 2,200. \par \par \uc2      The close broke a week-old record and is being attributed to \par \par \uc2  the return in massive numbers of small retail investors. \par \par \uc2      MALAYSIA POSTS ANOTHER BIG TRADE SURPLUS \par \par \uc2      Malaysia completed a 19-month streak of consecutive trade \par \par \uc2  surpluses when it released May numbers. These revealed a surplus \par \par \uc2  of 6.4 billion ringgit with January to May imports up 3.2 percent \par \par \uc2  and import levels still down 5.2 percent over the same period. \par \par \uc2      "Export growth is robust. Import growth has been constrained, \par \par \uc2  so overall the trade picture is very bullish," Lian said. \par \par \uc2      Malaysian shares did well on the news, ending up 2.98 percent \par \par \uc2  at 835.31. \par \par \uc2       Change on the day THU 01 1002GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...Latest bid....Prev Close....Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7995.......3.8000.........0.01% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......6825.00......6675.00........-2.20% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........36.73........36.85.........0.33% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........37.95........38.04.........0.24% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.6970.......1.6994.........0.14% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr...32.300.......32.290........-0.03% \par \par \uc2   Korean won..1164.00......1157.50........-0.56% \par \par \uc2   Japan yen....120.82.......121.03.........0.17% \par \par \uc2   Change since start of Asia crisis \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .....Latest......July '97......Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7995.......2.5200........-33.68% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......6825.00......2432.00........-64.37% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........36.85........25.90........-29.72% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........37.95........26.50........-30.17% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.6970.......1.4300........-15.73% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr..32.3000......27.7500........-14.09% \par \par \uc2   Korean won..1164.00.......842.00........-27.66% \par \par \uc2   Japan yen....120.82.......114.40.......