\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Choppy Late; Brunei Report Damps Fed Move \b0\par\par\uc2 357 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juli 1999\par 10:13\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar fidgeted sharply in late Thursday trade in Asia, but remained stronger compared with levels a day earlier. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. Federal Reserve's decision Wednesday to return to a neutral monetary stance form a tightening bias has given the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength against the U.S. dollar by deflating any immediate hope of further rate cuts in the U.S. \par \par \uc2  However, that sentiment was buffeted in midafternoon trading by a large corporate order to buy U.S. dollars, and news of a forthcoming report by Asiaweek magazine that Brunei's foreign reserves have almost been deleted. \par \par \uc2  About 0800 GMT (4 a.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.6975, down from S$1.7003 in late Asian trade Wednesday. About an hour earlier, it had peaked momentarily at S$1.7047. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the spike was caused by an order from a Singapore-based company to buy U.S. dollars and by news of the upcoming magazine report on Brunei. \par \par \uc2  Asiaweek reportedly estimates in this week's edition that Brunei's foreign reserves have fallen to US$5 billion from US$30 billion. A summary of the story was released ahead of publication. \par \par \uc2  "Brunei stories always effect Singapore, but it's kind of a muted effect," one trader said, noting the Singapore dollar movement was relatively small. \par \par \uc2  Brunei and Singapore have pegged their dollars at parity since 1967 by mutual agreement, and bad economic news for Brunei tends to put pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar. \par \par \uc2  Although the market is watching out for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  at these levels, traders said there is so far no sign of the authority moving to curb Singapore dollar strength. \par \par \uc2  On the local money market, the interbank overnight rate was offered at 1.250%, down from 1.750% late Wednesday in Asia, while the three-month rate was offered at 1.5625%, down from 1.6875% late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  -By Roger Malone; 65/421-4800; roger.malone@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 01-07-99 \par \par \uc2  0813GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv7104z41\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
