\par\par \b \uc2  EMERGING MARKET  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asia balancing act,Europe quiet. \b0\par\par\uc2 886 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juni 1999\par 13:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 23 (Reuters) - Emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept up their balancing act on Wednesday, caught between investor bullishness and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  concern over exports. \par \par \uc2  Central European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were quiet, with the Polish zloty tipped to test resistance at five percent above its basket parity and the Czech crown becalmed ahead of Thursday's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board meeting. \par \par \uc2  Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were slightly softer from late New York levels, with central banks divided on how to cope with the regionals' recent surge. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Korea \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again to buy dollar/won, and analysts said there was talk the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar strength. \par \par \uc2  But the baht hit a five-month high on Tuesday after the Bank of Thailand said it would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to restrain the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise. \par \par \uc2  "Their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are strengthening to the extent that some are definitely starting to impinge on export growth, or even cause export contraction," said Callum Henderson, emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Citibank in London. \par \par \uc2  "They seem to be trying to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and as a result continuing to offer the market good opportunities to sell into any rallies." \par \par \uc2  But he noted that Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stopped \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to damp down the Taiwan dollar a couple of weeks ago, and was now acting only to smooth out market moves. \par \par \uc2  "You could argue that one by one the Asian central banks have seen the writing on the wall and are giving up," he said. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were still showing little correlation with movements in dollar/yen, which firmed back through 122 in the London morning. \par \par \uc2  "This is largely a reflection of the strength of Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and the underlying demand for them," analysts at Banque Paribas said in a briefing note. \par \par \uc2  "As authorities' confidence in the economic recovery improves, gradual \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength will be tolerated." \par \par \uc2  The won was slightly weaker on the day after the Bank of Korea waded back in to buy an estimated $350 million. \par \par \uc2  The baht also lost some ground after rating agency Moody's slammed Thai banks, saying the sector was still in deep crisis. The Philippine peso tracked the baht lower, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah tried to press on towards 6,500 to the dollar but got stuck around 6,700 as profit-taking trimmed earlier gains, despite upbeat comments by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Syahril Sabirin that he would be happy with a stable range of 6,000-6,500. \par \par \uc2  In Europe, the zloty edged up to around 4.8 percent above its basket parity from Tuesday's 4.7 percent. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has gained two percentage points against the basket in June alone, would soon test five percent amid expectations that the $1 billion privatisation of Pekao bank would bring in large foreign inflows. \par \par \uc2  Data showing Poland's gross domestic product grew by 1.5 percent in the first quarter of the year had no immediate impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Analysts said the figures were close to expectations and were already discounted. \par \par \uc2  The Hungarian forint held steady near the top of its 4.5 percent-wide trading band and the Czech crown barely moved ahead of Thursday's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board meeting, when analysts expect a minor interest rate cut. ** Following is a table of key emerging market exchange rates, including the change versus late New York trade the previous day and the change in the year to date.. ** The Czech, Polish, Hungarian and Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , formerly quoted against the mark, are now quoted against the euro to reflect new market norms. All other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are quoted against the dollar. ** According to market convention, exchange rates are quoted in units per dollar or euro and the percentage change denotes the rise or fall of the dollar or euro value. ** Annual percentage changes are calculated from late on the first day of the current trading year, January 4. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab \tab     LATEST  PREV    PCT CHG  PCT CHG\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   CLOSE\tab \tab in 1999\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par EUROPE/MEAST/AFRICA\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Czech Rep.\tab \tab     36.84   36.81    0.08%   5.85%\par  Poland\tab \tab \tab    4.03    4.03    0.02%  -0.91%\par  Hungary\tab \tab \tab 249.11  249.18   -0.03%  -0.83%\par  Slovakia\tab \tab \tab 45.22   45.25   -0.07%   5.16%\par  Romania\tab \tab \tab 15,725  15,690    0.22%  43.6