\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA MARKETS-Won off on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 , rupiah gains. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Ritsuko Ando \par \uc2 886 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juni 1999\par 11:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , June 23 (Reuters) - Regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  shrugged \par \par \uc2  off the yen's softer bias on Wednesday, while the South Korean \par \par \uc2  won was dragged to a lower close on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at \par \par \uc2  protecting South Korean exports. \par \par \uc2      Asian shares finished mixed. Singapore shares gained more \par \par \uc2  than two percent and Korean shares nearly one and a half \par \par \uc2  percent, while Thailand and Taiwan shares declined by more than \par \par \uc2  one percent. \par \par \uc2      KOREAN WON CLOSES WEAKER ON LAST MINUTE \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2      The South Korean won finished weaker against the dollar \par \par \uc2  after verbal and physical \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      Dealers said the Bank of Korea stepped in to buy dollars at \par \par \uc2  both the opening and the closing of trade. The won finished at \par \par \uc2  1,162.8, compared with Tuesday's 1,159.4. \par \par \uc2      A finance ministry official said the government would take \par \par \uc2  steps to rein in the won, saying its appreciation was \par \par \uc2  undesirable when the yen was continuing to depreciate against \par \par \uc2  the dollar. \par \par \uc2      Catherine Tan, managing analyst for Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at \par \par \uc2  Thomson Global Markets in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  would not likely have a lasting effect. \par \par \uc2      "Eventually the government is not going to win the fight \par \par \uc2  against the market sentiment due to the huge influx of funds," \par \par \uc2  she said. \par \par \uc2      A weaker yen is perceived to be a potential threat to \par \par \uc2  Korea's export manufacturers, as it would boost Japan's export \par \par \uc2  competitiveness. \par \par \uc2      RUPIAH HEADED EVEN STRONGER, SAYS INDONESIAN C.BANKER \par \par \uc2      The Indonesian rupiah continued to shine after yesterday's \par \par \uc2  move through 7,000, inching towards 6,500 to the dollar as \par \par \uc2  overseas money continued to flow in. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Syahril Sabirin told reporters that \par \par \uc2  the rupiah could strengthen to 6,000 to the dollar, saying he \par \par \uc2  would be happy with a stable range of 6,000 to 6,500. \par \par \uc2      "I cannot predict what the level is, but the possibility \par \par \uc2  for strengthening is there," he said before a meeting with \par \par \uc2  President B.J. Habibie. \par \par \uc2      "We have calculated that the level of 6,000-6,500 is okay \par \par \uc2  for exports," he said. \par \par \uc2      MALAYSIAN Q1 GDP EXPECTED TO SHOW CONTRACTION \par \par \uc2      Malaysian first quarter GDP, due at 1030 GMT, is expected \par \par \uc2  to show a contraction of 1.6 percent year-on-year in the first \par \par \uc2  quarter. \par \par \uc2      Prime Minister Mahathir Mohamad said on June 9 that GDP \par \par \uc2  shrank by that amount, but that GDP was likely to expand in the \par \par \uc2  second quarter. \par \par \uc2      But even the first quarter GDP growth figure given by the \par \par \uc2  prime minister would compare favourably with the 8.10 percent \par \par \uc2  contraction in the final quarter of last year. \par \par \uc2      TAIPEI STOCK RALLY HALTS, \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  DEALERS SIDELINED \par \par \uc2      Taiwan released unemployment figures for May, which showed \par \par \uc2  a 2.84 percent rate, up from April's 2.75 percent. The rise was \par \par \uc2  sharper than most market expectations. \par \par \uc2      An official said the June jobless rate may be even higher, \par \par \uc2  and might exceed three percent in July and August before easing \par \par \uc2  back in September. \par \par \uc2      But he said that since unemployment numbers were a lagging \par \par \uc2  indicator, the latest figures should not be interpreted as a \par \par \uc2  negative sign for the country's economic recovery. \par \par \uc2      Taipei shares finished lower for the first time in four \par \par \uc2  days, as profit-taking in the heavily weighted electronics \par \par \uc2  sector halted the market's rally. \par \par \uc2      The Taiwan dollar closed unchanged, with investors stepping \par \par \uc2  to the sidelines as they detected some \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves to \par \par \uc2  limit its upside. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  Change on the day WED 23 0907GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...Latest bid....Prev Close....Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7995.......3.8000..........0.01% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......6675.00......6750.00..........1.12% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........36.69........36.61.........-0.22% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........37.84........37.79.........-0.13% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.7020.......1.7030..........0.06% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr...32.335.......32.310.........-0.08% \par \par \uc2   Korean won..1161.00......1158.00.........-0.26% \par \par \uc2   Japan yen....122.08.......121.75.........-0.27% \par \par \uc2   Change since start of Asia crisis \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .....Latest......July '97......Pct Move